IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Regulation Crowdfunding`

-- The SEC's clock. Filings, offering deadlines, cancellation windows and the
-- 21-day publication floor are all dated on the Commission's own business
-- calendar, which runs on Eastern time.
--
-- CAVEAT, because this is world knowledge and not bundle knowledge: 17 CFR
-- part 227 fixes NO timezone anywhere. "America/New_York" is the EDGAR/SEC
-- convention, taken here because `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` outside an
-- `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` scope needs a zone to localise today, and a
-- zone had to be chosen. It is a convention, not a rule, and it belongs in the
-- fork register as such.
TIMEZONE IS "America/New_York"

-- ===========================================================================
-- 17 CFR PART 227 — REGULATION CROWDFUNDING, as in force from 2023-03-01.
--
-- SCOPE. All 22 sections of the part are addressed: §§ 227.100, 201-206,
-- 300-305, 400-404 and 501-504. Where a section is encoded at reduced surface
-- the reduction is stated at the site, in the section's own §§ block, and not
-- only here.
--
-- SOURCES. Every quoted string is verbatim from
--   jl4/examples/legal/regcf/denovo/source/part227.txt
-- (sha256 a2ddacb76c97006abca1d6f590ebce3259de562995cbf5a82c2d4f7219ba06e2),
-- the provenance-headed assembly of the eCFR versioner's own XML rendering of
-- the part as of 2026-08-03, deposited by P1 with the bundle at
-- ../denovo/source-bundle.json. eCFR italics are written _like this_ in the
-- source; the underscores are dropped from the quotes here.
--
-- CURRENCY. The eCFR versioner reports title 17 up to date as of 2026-08-03
-- and part 227's own latest_amendment_date as 2023-03-01. P2's sweep
-- (../denovo/external-modifications.json) independently confirmed no Federal
-- Register document has amended the part since, and no court has struck,
-- stayed or read down any provision of it.
--
-- MODELLING NOTE. Constitutive material — who is exempt, what the limits are,
-- who is disqualified, what a term means — is `DECIDE`/`MEANS` predicates
-- carrying the regulation's own words in the FIELD NAMES, with the paragraph
-- label riding beside its node as a truncated inert string joined by `...`.
-- Regulative material — who must file what, by when, and what happens if they
-- do not — is `PARTY … MUST/MAY/SHANT … WITHIN … HENCE/LEST`. Ten provisions
-- are BOTH: a duty whose content is a list (§§ 227.201, 202(a), 302(b)(1),
-- 303(d), 303(f)(1), 304(b)(2), 404(a), 204(b), 206(b), 303(b)(2)). Each of
-- those is split into a constitutive COMPLETENESS PREDICATE naming every item
-- as a field, and a regulative rule carrying that predicate as a `PROVIDED`
-- guard — so the content list is where an engine can execute it and the party
-- and deadline are where a process diagram can draw them. That split is an
-- encoding choice, not the text's; the alternative (one obligation per item,
-- 25 of them for § 227.201) is defensible and is registered as such.
--
-- INERT STRINGS. Under the enumeration-label ruling an inert string that
-- merely restates the node beside it is deleted — inert never shadows active.
-- A verbatim quotation survives ONLY where no active node carries its words:
-- a closed permitted-content list referenced elsewhere only by cross-reference
-- (§ 227.204(b)(1)-(3)), a pure definition carrier (§ 227.204(e),
-- § 227.305(b)), and a chapeau whose substance the limbs below it do not
-- repeat.
--
-- FACTS. Threaded as GIVEN records, never as top-level ASSUME. The one
-- module-level ASSUME is a deliberate refusal bottom (see the encoding floor
-- below), which is what ASSUME is good for.
--
-- WHAT IS OUT OF SCOPE, and why:
--   * FORMS. §§ 239.900 (Form C, C/A, C-U, C-AR, C-AR/A, C-TR) and 249.2000
--     (Form Funding Portal) prescribe forms, not tests. P1 deliberately did
--     not capture them. Filing EVENTS are modelled; form CONTENTS beyond what
--     § 227.201 itself enumerates are not.
--   * § 227.100(e) INTEGRATION. A bare pointer to § 230.152, which the bundle
--     does not carry. Encoded as a pointer, not expanded.
--   * § 230.501(a) at REDUCED SURFACE. Categories (1)-(4) and (7)-(13) turn on
--     institutional status and entity asset tests that part 227 never uses
--     arithmetically; they arrive as one already-construed boolean input with
--     an @ref. Categories (5) (net worth) and (6) (income) ARE encoded,
--     because Instruction 1 to § 227.100(a)(2) routes the investment-limit
--     arithmetic through them.
--   * The HISTORIC TEXT of the part. P2's warning is load-bearing: the bundle
--     captured only the text in force from 2023-03-01. The DATES of every
--     historic arm are known; the superseded WORDS are not, and an arm that
--     appeared to carry them would be fabricated. So: one dated arm, opening
--     2022-09-20, and a refusal floor below it.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Interpretation — the six readings this encoding is parameterised on`

-- P2's sweep found six places where an SEC staff interpretation says something
-- the regulation's own words do not. Each is a genuine fork: two readings that
-- disagree on a population that exists. Rather than pick one and present it as
-- the text, the encoding takes the reading as a PARAMETER — one Interpretation
-- record threaded through every decision that depends on it. Two named values
-- of that record are supplied below: `the staff reading`, which resolves every
-- fork the way the SEC staff has, and `the text alone`, which resolves every
-- fork on the regulation's own words. The gap between the two answers IS the
-- measurable content of the forks.
--
-- The six ids are the P2 -> P4 contract: F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL,
-- F-CAP-12MONTH-ANCHOR, F-ANNUAL-INCOME-PERIOD, F-REPORTING-DISQUALIFICATION,
-- F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD, F-ONE-INTERMEDIARY-SCOPE.

@ref F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL; § 227.100(a)(2) and Instruction 1 thereto; CFI 100.02 [Mar. 12, 2025]
DECLARE `non-natural investor limit reading` IS ONE OF
    `revenue or net assets`
    `annual income or net worth`

@ref F-CAP-12MONTH-ANCHOR; § 227.100(a)(1); CFI 100.05 [Feb. 17, 2026]; intermediary FAQ 304.3
DECLARE `twelve month window reading` IS ONE OF
    `rolling from each closing`
    `from the date of such offer or sale`

@ref F-ANNUAL-INCOME-PERIOD; § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 1; § 230.501(a)(6); CFI 100.06 [Feb. 17, 2026]
DECLARE `annual income period reading` IS ONE OF
    `the calendar year`
    `the investor's own fiscal year`

@ref F-REPORTING-DISQUALIFICATION; § 227.100(b)(2); CFI 100.04 [Feb. 17, 2026]
DECLARE `reporting disqualification reading` IS ONE OF
    `presently subject to the reporting requirement`
    `ever subject to the reporting requirement`

@ref F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD; § 227.202(b)(2) against § 227.100(d); CFI 202.02 [Jul. 9, 2026]
DECLARE `holders of record reading` IS ONE OF
    `the investors who invested in the offering`
    `the register of holders of record`

@ref F-ONE-INTERMEDIARY-SCOPE; Instruction to § 227.100(a)(3); CFI 100.03 [Feb. 17, 2026]
DECLARE `one intermediary scope reading` IS ONE OF
    `the prohibition binds the offering`
    `the prohibition binds the issuer`

-- MEASURED 2026-08-05: `TYPICALLY` will not carry these defaults. The
-- typechecker requires a TYPICALLY value to be "a number, a string, or a
-- nullary constructor such as TRUE, FALSE or NOTHING", and a user-declared
-- nullary constructor is refused. So the defaults live below as the two named
-- Interpretation values instead of on the fields, which is arguably better
-- anyway: `the staff reading` is one word for a caller to write, and the
-- opposite pole gets a name too.
@ref P2 -> P4 fork contract, ../denovo/external-modifications.json
DECLARE Interpretation HAS
    `non-natural investor limit basis` IS A  `non-natural investor limit reading`
    `twelve month window anchor`       IS A  `twelve month window reading`
    `annual income period`             IS AN `annual income period reading`
    `reporting disqualification tense` IS A  `reporting disqualification reading`
    `holders of record basis`          IS A  `holders of record reading`
    `one intermediary scope`           IS A  `one intermediary scope reading`

-- The staff reading of every fork, as one value, so a caller who wants "what
-- would the SEC say" writes one word.
@ref the six Corporation Finance Interpretations and the Trading and Markets FAQ named above
GIVETH AN Interpretation
`the staff reading` MEANS Interpretation WITH
    `non-natural investor limit basis` IS `revenue or net assets`
    `twelve month window anchor`       IS `rolling from each closing`
    `annual income period`             IS `the calendar year`
    `reporting disqualification tense` IS `presently subject to the reporting requirement`
    `holders of record basis`          IS `the investors who invested in the offering`
    `one intermediary scope`           IS `the prohibition binds the offering`

-- The other pole: every fork resolved by the regulation's own words, with no
-- interpretive help. Not "wrong" — it is what a reader of the CFR alone would
-- compute, and the gap between the two is the measurable content of the forks.
@ref 17 CFR part 227, the enacted text alone
GIVETH AN Interpretation
`the text alone` MEANS Interpretation WITH
    `non-natural investor limit basis` IS `annual income or net worth`
    `twelve month window anchor`       IS `from the date of such offer or sale`
    `annual income period`             IS `the investor's own fiscal year`
    `reporting disqualification tense` IS `ever subject to the reporting requirement`
    `holders of record basis`          IS `the register of holders of record`
    `one intermediary scope`           IS `the prohibition binds the issuer`


§§ `The rule-version axis — the seven inflation-indexed constants`

-- Securities Act § 4A(h)(1) (15 U.S.C. 77d-1(h)(1)) requires every dollar
-- amount used in connection with the crowdfunding exemption to be adjusted for
-- CPI-U "not less frequently than once every five years". The Commission has
-- done it twice: Release 33-10332 (effective 2017-04-12) and Release 33-11098
-- (effective 2022-09-20). The current figures are therefore already in their
-- fourth year and the next adjustment falls due by about September 2027. No
-- adjustment has been proposed.
--
-- So the seven figures go on the rule-version axis NOW, as ONE dated arm, even
-- though only one arm can be written. The point is that the next indexation
-- becomes an ADDED ARM rather than an edited literal.
--
-- WHY THERE IS NO 2017 ARM. The bundle captured only the text in force from
-- 2023-03-01. The 2017 figures live in the Federal Register granule the
-- bundle's annotation inventory names under marker FR2017Apr12 (82 FR 17552,
-- Release 33-10332) and are NOT in evidence here. Writing them from memory
-- would be fabrication, so the arm below them is a refusal, not a number.
--
-- THE DELIBERATE TENSION, stated so a reader does not mistake it for a bug:
-- the arm opens 2022-09-20 but the encoding floor is 2023-03-01. Both are
-- true. The figures are known from the 2022 release; but between those two
-- dates the part also carried three COVID-era provisions — § 227.201(bb),
-- § 227.301(e) and a live § 227.100(b)(7) — whose text the bundle does not
-- hold. The seven constants below are right for any date from 2022-09-20; the
-- REST of this module is only right from 2023-03-01, and the floor says so.

@ref Release Nos. 33-11098; 34-95715, 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022), effective Sept. 20, 2022
GIVETH A DATE
`the 2022 inflation adjustment` MEANS YMD 2022 9 20

-- Below this date the module has no text to encode from. Reaching this
-- binding stops evaluation loudly and names itself, which is the whole point:
-- a curated refusal beats a silently wrong number.
ASSUME `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20` IS A NUMBER

@ref eCFR versioner diff of 2023-02-28 against 2023-03-02; 86 FR 3590/3591/3592 sunset
GIVETH A DATE
`the lapse of the COVID-era provisions` MEANS YMD 2023 3 1

GIVEN change IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rules in force include` change MEANS
    `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST change

@ref § 227.100(a)(1); 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate offering cap` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 5_000_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(i); 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investor floor` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 2_500
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

-- Roles 3, 4 and 5 are all $124,000 today and are three separate constants,
-- because nothing guarantees the next release moves them together.
@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(i)-(ii) — the income/net-worth tier boundary; 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investor tier boundary` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 124_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(ii) — the absolute ceiling on the ten percent arm; 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investor ceiling` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 124_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

@ref § 227.201(t)(1) — upper bound of the tax-return-information tier; 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax return information ceiling` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 124_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

@ref § 227.201(t)(2)-(3) — upper bound of the reviewed tier; 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reviewed statements ceiling` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 618_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`

@ref § 227.201(t)(3) proviso — the first-time-issuer reviewed ceiling; 87 FR 57394, 57398 (Sept. 20, 2022)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first-time issuer reviewed ceiling` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 1_235_000
           OTHERWISE `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`


