§§ `Business days — a measured gap in the toolchain, recorded not papered over`

-- The part uses "business day" TWELVE times and never defines it; the single
-- mention of a holiday is Instruction 4 to § 227.201(t) ("If the 120th day
-- falls on a Saturday, Sunday, or holiday, the next business day shall be
-- considered the 120th day").
--
-- MEASURED 2026-08-05: `daydate` supplies `Weekday of` and `is weekend`, so
-- weekends ARE computable; NO holiday calendar exists in any L4 library —
-- /usr/bin/grep -rn over jl4-core/libraries/*.l4 for "business" and "holiday"
-- finds only ACTUS's `NoCalendar` enum constructor and an unrelated
-- jurisdiction string.
--
-- So the roll below skips WEEKENDS ONLY, and the federal-holiday calendar is
-- an open question routed to the fork register as a fact-convention: the
-- number of holidays intervening in the window arrives as a fact where a
-- provision needs it. Keeping the weekend arithmetic visible and the calendar
-- burden explicit beats delegating the whole computation to an already-resolved
-- date supplied by the fact-giver, which would hide the gap rather than record
-- it.

-- `the day after` comes from daydate.

@ref the twelve "business day" deadlines of this part; weekend roll only, holidays supplied as a fact
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      n        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`business days after` `the day` n MEANS
    BRANCH IF n AT MOST 0                     THEN `the day`
           IF `is weekend` (`the day after` `the day`)
                                              THEN `business days after` (`the day after` `the day`) n
           OTHERWISE                               `business days after` (`the day after` `the day`) (n MINUS 1)

@ref § 227.201(t) Instruction 4 — "If the 120th day falls on a Saturday, Sunday, or holiday, the next business day"
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`rolled forward off a weekend` `the day` MEANS
    IF   `is weekend` `the day`
    THEN `rolled forward off a weekend` (`the day after` `the day`)
    ELSE `the day`


§§ `Annex — § 230.501(a), the accredited-investor test, at reduced surface`

-- § 227.100(a)(2) applies its investment limits only "where the purchaser is
-- not an accredited investor (as defined in Rule 501 (§ 230.501 of this
-- chapter))", and Instruction 1 to that paragraph sends the annual-income and
-- net-worth CALCULATION to the same place. So § 230.501 is reached twice, for
-- two different jobs, and this module encodes it at two different depths.
--
--   * Categories (a)(1)-(4) and (a)(7)-(13) turn on institutional status,
--     entity type and entity asset tests that part 227 never uses
--     arithmetically. They arrive as ONE already-construed boolean input with
--     an @ref pointer — an input, not a stub. This is the BNA precedent for an
--     out-of-scope statutory concept.
--   * Categories (a)(5) (net worth) and (a)(6) (income) ARE encoded, including
--     the (a)(5)(i) primary-residence arithmetic and the (a)(5)(ii)
--     grandfather, because Instruction 1 to § 227.100(a)(2) routes the
--     investment-limit arithmetic through exactly those two.
--
-- Note that § 230.501 runs on its OWN amendment clock — its citation note ends
-- at 90 FR 9687 (Feb. 18, 2025), not at 87 FR 57398 — so its figures are NOT
-- among the seven that move together under 15 U.S.C. 77d-1(h)(1) and are not
-- on this module's rule-version axis.

@ref 17 CFR § 230.501(a)(5)-(6); § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 1; § 227.501(b)
DECLARE InvestorProfile HAS
    name                                                                            IS A STRING

    -- § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 1 speaks only of "a natural person"; the
    -- limb an entity investor falls into is fork F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL.
    `a natural person`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN

    -- The already-construed arm of § 230.501(a): categories (1)-(4), (7)-(13).
    `within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- F-ANNUAL-INCOME-PERIOD carried as a PAIR of inputs, so the fork is not
    -- hidden inside one number the fact-supplier chose the meaning of.
    `annual income for the calendar year`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `annual income for the investor's own fiscal year`                              IS A NUMBER

    -- F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL, likewise as a pair: the rule's own quantities and
    -- the interpretation's substituted quantities, side by side.
    `revenue for the most recent fiscal year`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end`                              IS A NUMBER

    -- § 230.501(a)(5)(i) components. Net worth is COMPUTED from these below;
    -- there is no "net worth" input, because the whole content of (a)(5)(i) is
    -- how to compute it.
    `total assets other than the primary residence`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence`    IS A NUMBER
    `estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale`  IS A NUMBER
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale`  IS A NUMBER
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale`  IS A NUMBER
    `the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- § 230.501(a)(5)(ii), the grandfather. When it applies, (a)(5)(i) does
    -- not, and the unadjusted figure governs.
    `the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments`              IS A NUMBER

    -- § 230.501(a)(6).
    `individual income in each of the two most recent years`                        IS A NUMBER
    `joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years`       IS A NUMBER
    `a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- § 227.100(a)(2) and its Instruction 2.
    `aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months`  IS A NUMBER
    `annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate investment of the investor spouses`                              IS A NUMBER

@ref § 230.501(a)(5)(i)(C) — indebtedness in excess of the fair market value is a liability
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`(C) — the indebtedness in excess of the fair market value` investor MEANS
    max 0 (      investor's `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale`
           MINUS investor's `estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale`)

-- AMBIGUITY: (B) subtracts mortgage debt up to fair market value from the
-- liability side, "except that if the amount ... outstanding at the time of
-- sale ... exceeds the amount outstanding 60 days before such time, other than
-- as a result of the acquisition of the primary residence, the amount of such
-- excess shall be included as a liability". Where the mortgage BOTH exceeds
-- fair market value AND grew in the last 60 days, the excess over fair market
-- value can be counted twice — once by (C) and once by (B)'s exception.
-- Reading (i): the two limbs are cumulative, as the words say (taken here).
-- Reading (ii): (C) subsumes the overlap and only the non-overlapping part of
-- (B)'s excess counts. The text supplies no netting rule and this encoding
-- does not invent one.
@ref § 230.501(a)(5)(i)(B) — the 60-day increase in indebtedness is a liability
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`(B) — the increase in the indebtedness in the 60 days before the sale` investor MEANS
    IF   investor's `the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence`
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (      investor's `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale`
                MINUS investor's `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale`)

@ref § 230.501(a)(5)(i) — "(A) The person's primary residence shall not be included as an asset"
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`net worth computed under paragraph (a)(5)(i)` investor MEANS
          investor's `total assets other than the primary residence`
    MINUS investor's `total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence`
    MINUS `(C) — the indebtedness in excess of the fair market value` investor
    MINUS `(B) — the increase in the indebtedness in the 60 days before the sale` investor

@ref § 230.501(a)(5)(ii)(A)-(C) — the July 20, 2010 grandfather
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (a)(5)(i) does not apply to this calculation` investor MEANS
        investor's `the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities`
    AND "(A)" ... investor's `that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010`
    AND "(B)" ... investor's `qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired`
    AND "(C)" ... investor's `held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010`

@ref § 230.501(a)(5) — "individual net worth, or joint net worth with that person's spouse or spousal equivalent"
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investor's net worth` investor MEANS
    IF   `paragraph (a)(5)(i) does not apply to this calculation` investor
    THEN investor's `net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments`
    ELSE `net worth computed under paragraph (a)(5)(i)` investor

@ref § 230.501(a)(5) — "exceeds $1,000,000"
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(a)(5) — net worth exceeds one million dollars` investor MEANS
        "(5)" ... `the investor's net worth` investor GREATER THAN `the accredited investor net worth threshold`

@ref § 230.501(a)(6) — the income test
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(a)(6) — income in each of the two most recent years` investor MEANS
        "(6)" ... (    investor's `individual income in each of the two most recent years` GREATER THAN `the accredited investor individual income threshold`
                   OR  investor's `joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years` GREATER THAN `the accredited investor joint income threshold`)
    AND investor's `a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year`

-- § 227.501(b) restates the § 230.501(a) test locally for resales, adding "or
-- who the seller reasonably believes comes within any of such categories" —
-- the same reasonable-belief limb § 230.501(a)'s own chapeau carries for the
-- issuer. Both are folded into the already-construed input field, whose name
-- says "or reasonably believed to be".
@ref § 230.501(a) chapeau; § 227.501(b)
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investor is an accredited investor` investor IF
        investor's `within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be`
    ..  (`(a)(5) — net worth exceeds one million dollars` investor AND investor's `a natural person`)
    ..  (`(a)(6) — income in each of the two most recent years` investor AND investor's `a natural person`)


§§ `Annex — § 270.3a-9, the crowdfunding vehicle`

-- Reached by § 227.100(d): "A crowdfunding vehicle (as defined in § 270.3a-9
-- of this chapter) is not considered an investor for the purposes of this
-- part." The nine conditions of § 270.3a-9(a) are what make an entity a
-- crowdfunding vehicle that is deemed not to be an investment company; they
-- are encoded because the exclusion in § 227.100(d) turns on them, and because
-- they collide with § 227.202(b)(2) at fork F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD.

@ref 17 CFR § 270.3a-9(a)(1)-(9)
DECLARE `Crowdfunding vehicle` HAS
    name                                                                            IS A STRING
    `organized and operated for the sole purpose of directly acquiring, holding, and disposing of securities issued by a single crowdfunding issuer and raising capital in one or more Regulation Crowdfunding offerings`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `does not borrow money and uses the proceeds solely to purchase a single class of securities of a single crowdfunding issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `issues only one class of securities in offerings in which the vehicle and the crowdfunding issuer are deemed co-issuers`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives a written undertaking from the crowdfunding issuer to fund or reimburse its expenses, receives no other compensation, and any compensation paid to any person operating it is paid solely by the crowdfunding issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintains the same fiscal year-end as the crowdfunding issuer`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintains a one-to-one relationship between the crowdfunding issuer securities it owns and its own securities outstanding`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `seeks instructions from the holders of its securities on voting and on tender or exchange offers, and acts only in accordance with those instructions`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives all Regulation Crowdfunding disclosures from the crowdfunding issuer and promptly provides them to its investors and to the relevant intermediary`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides each investor the right to direct it to assert the rights the investor would have had if he or she had invested directly`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 17 CFR § 270.3a-9(a) — the nine conjunctive conditions
GIVEN vehicle IS A `Crowdfunding vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a crowdfunding vehicle deemed not to be an investment company` vehicle IF
        "(1)" ... vehicle's `organized and operated for the sole purpose of directly acquiring, holding, and disposing of securities issued by a single crowdfunding issuer and raising capital in one or more Regulation Crowdfunding offerings`
    ... "(2)" ... vehicle's `does not borrow money and uses the proceeds solely to purchase a single class of securities of a single crowdfunding issuer`
    ... "(3)" ... vehicle's `issues only one class of securities in offerings in which the vehicle and the crowdfunding issuer are deemed co-issuers`
    ... "(4)" ... vehicle's `receives a written undertaking from the crowdfunding issuer to fund or reimburse its expenses, receives no other compensation, and any compensation paid to any person operating it is paid solely by the crowdfunding issuer`
    ... "(5)" ... vehicle's `maintains the same fiscal year-end as the crowdfunding issuer`
    ... "(6)" ... vehicle's `maintains a one-to-one relationship between the crowdfunding issuer securities it owns and its own securities outstanding`
    ... "(7)" ... vehicle's `seeks instructions from the holders of its securities on voting and on tender or exchange offers, and acts only in accordance with those instructions`
    ... "(8)" ... vehicle's `receives all Regulation Crowdfunding disclosures from the crowdfunding issuer and promptly provides them to its investors and to the relevant intermediary`
    ... "(9)" ... vehicle's `provides each investor the right to direct it to assert the rights the investor would have had if he or she had invested directly`


§§ `The facts — one record per thing the regulation asks a question about`

-- Nine more records. Every field name carries the regulation's own words, with
-- the verb dropped where the genitive `'s` already supplies it: a field is
-- `to the issuer of the securities`, never `is to the issuer of the securities`.

