§§ `§ 227.503 Disqualification provisions`

-- ENCODED BEFORE § 227.100 because § 227.100(b)(4) calls it: an issuer is
-- ineligible if it "is not eligible ... as a result of a disqualification as
-- specified in § 227.503(a)". Citation order would put § 227.100 first; the
-- dependency runs the other way, and the general rule this module follows is:
-- a cross-reference to another rule's OUTCOME is a call, a cross-reference to
-- another rule's COMPLIANCE is an input field. § 227.100(b)(4) asks for
-- § 227.503(a)'s outcome, so it is a call, so § 227.503 comes first.
--
-- STRUCTURE. Eight classes of covered person (the chapeau) crossed with eight
-- event limbs (a)(1)-(a)(8), each with its own lookback and its own anchor.
-- The transition in (b)(1) is applied PER EVENT rather than once at the end,
-- because that is what its words do: "with respect to any conviction, order,
-- judgment, decree, suspension, expulsion or bar that occurred or was issued
-- before May 16, 2016".
--
-- AMBIGUITY (a)(1) counts its lookback from "the filing of the offering
-- statement or such sale"; (a)(2), (a)(3)(ii), (a)(5), (a)(7) and (a)(8) count
-- theirs from "the filing of the information required by section 4A(b) of the
-- Securities Act". Both are, in practice, Form C. Reading (i): the two phrases
-- name the same event and one anchor date serves both (taken here — a single
-- `the filing` parameter). Reading (ii): they are distinct, because § 227.201
-- and section 4A(b) are separately enumerated elsewhere in this part. Not
-- resolved by the text.
--
-- AMBIGUITY the chapeau tests a promoter "at the time of filing, any offer
-- after filing, or such sale", and the Instruction to paragraph (a) tests a
-- twenty percent beneficial owner "only as of the time of filing of the
-- offering statement and not from the time of such sale". Whether the other
-- six classes are tested continuously between filing and sale is not stated.
-- Reading (i): one anchor date per evaluation, supplied by the caller, and the
-- Instruction's narrowing is honoured by evaluating owners at the filing date
-- (taken here). Reading (ii): a per-class anchor. Not resolved by the text.

@ref the lookback windows of § 227.503(a); daydate footgun — decrement the YEAR, never subtract months
GIVEN `the anchor` IS A DATE
      `years`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date that many years earlier` `the anchor` `years` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the anchor`) (DATE_MONTH `the anchor`) (DATE_YEAR `the anchor` MINUS `years`)

GIVEN `the event`  IS A DATE
      `the anchor` IS A DATE
      `years`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls within the lookback of` `the event` `the anchor` `years` MEANS
    `the event` AT LEAST (`the date that many years earlier` `the anchor` `years`)

@ref § 227.503(b)(1) — "any conviction, order, judgment, decree, suspension, expulsion or bar that occurred or was issued before May 16, 2016"
GIVEN `the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1)` `the event` MEANS
    `the event` AT LEAST `the disqualification transition date`

@ref § 227.503(a)(1) — "(or five years, in the case of issuers, their predecessors and affiliated issuers)"
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the conviction lookback in years` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person's class
    WHEN `the issuer itself`           THEN `the five year disqualification lookback`
    WHEN `a predecessor of the issuer` THEN `the five year disqualification lookback`
    WHEN `an affiliated issuer`        THEN `the five year disqualification lookback`
    OTHERWISE                               `the ten year disqualification lookback`

@ref § 227.503(a)(1)(i)-(iii)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conviction is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii)` person MEANS
        "(i)"   ... person's `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor in connection with the purchase or sale of any security`
    ..  "(ii)"  ... person's `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor involving the making of a false filing with the Commission`
    ..  "(iii)" ... person's `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities`

@ref § 227.503(a)(1)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
      `the filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`503(a)(1) — a disqualifying conviction` person `the filing` MEANS
        "(1)" ... `the conviction is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii)` person
    AND `falls within the lookback of` (person's `date of the conviction`) `the filing` (`the conviction lookback in years` person)
    AND `not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1)` (person's `date of the conviction`)

@ref § 227.503(a)(2)(i)-(iii)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court order is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii)` person MEANS
        "(i)"   ... person's `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct in connection with the purchase or sale of any security`
    ..  "(ii)"  ... person's `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct involving the making of a false filing with the Commission`
    ..  "(iii)" ... person's `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities`

@ref § 227.503(a)(2)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
      `the filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`503(a)(2) — a court order restraining or enjoining` person `the filing` MEANS
        "(2)" ... `the court order is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii)` person
    AND person's `the court order, judgment or decree restrains or enjoins the person at the time of such filing or sale`
    AND `falls within the lookback of` (person's `date the court order, judgment or decree was entered`) `the filing` `the five year disqualification lookback`
    AND `not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1)` (person's `date the court order, judgment or decree was entered`)

@ref § 227.503(a)(3)(i)(A)-(C)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the final order bars the person as described in (A), (B) or (C)` person MEANS
        "(A)" ... person's `that final order bars the person from association with an entity regulated by such commission, authority, agency or officer`
    ..  "(B)" ... person's `that final order bars the person from engaging in the business of securities, insurance or banking`
    ..  "(C)" ... person's `that final order bars the person from engaging in savings association or credit union activities`

-- (a)(3) has TWO limbs with DIFFERENT temporal shapes: (i) is a status test at
-- the time of filing or sale with no lookback at all, (ii) is an event test
-- with a TEN-year lookback. Only (ii) carries a window.
@ref § 227.503(a)(3)(ii) — "entered within ten years before such filing of the offering statement or such sale"
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
      `the filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the final order is a fraud-based order within ten years` person `the filing` MEANS
        "(ii)" ... person's `that final order is based on a violation of a law or regulation prohibiting fraudulent, manipulative or deceptive conduct`
    AND `falls within the lookback of` (person's `date the final order was entered`) `the filing` `the ten year disqualification lookback`

@ref § 227.503(a)(3)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
      `the filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`503(a)(3) — a final order of a State or Federal regulator` person `the filing` MEANS
        "(3)" ... person's `subject to a final order of a State securities commission, a State bank or credit union supervisor, a State insurance commission, an appropriate Federal banking agency, the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission or the National Credit Union Administration`
    AND (    "(i)" ... `the final order bars the person as described in (A), (B) or (C)` person
         ..  `the final order is a fraud-based order within ten years` person `the filing`)
    AND `not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1)` (person's `date the final order was entered`)

@ref § 227.503(a)(4)(i)-(iii)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Commission order does what (i), (ii) or (iii) describes` person MEANS
        "(i)"   ... person's `that Commission order suspends or revokes the person's registration as a broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser or funding portal`
    ..  "(ii)"  ... person's `that Commission order places limitations on the activities, functions or operations of the person`
    ..  "(iii)" ... person's `that Commission order bars the person from being associated with any entity or from participating in the offering of any penny stock`

