@ref § 227.503(a) with (b)(3) and (c)
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson
      `the filing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the covered person is disqualified` person `the filing` IF
        `a disqualifying event has occurred with respect to the covered person` person `the filing`
    AND NOT "(3)" ... person's `the court or regulatory authority that entered the relevant order, judgment or decree advised in writing that disqualification should not arise`
    AND NOT `503(c) — the event is excused as a pre-affiliation event of an affiliated issuer` person

-- The issuer-level test. (b)(2) — a Commission waiver on a showing of good
-- cause — and (b)(4) — the reasonable-care exception — are issuer-level, not
-- person-level, so they sit here and not in the predicate above.
@ref § 227.503(a) chapeau with (b)(2) and (b)(4)
GIVEN issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no exemption is available because of a disqualification` issuer IF
        any (`is disqualified at the filing date`) (issuer's `covered persons`)
    AND NOT "(2)" ... issuer's `the Commission has determined that it is not necessary under the circumstances that an exemption be denied`
    AND NOT "(4)" ... issuer's `did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known that a disqualification existed`
    WHERE
        `is disqualified at the filing date` person MEANS
            `the covered person is disqualified` person (issuer's `date the offering statement was filed`)

@ref § 227.503(d) — a person subject to a statutory disqualification may not act as, or be an associated person of, an intermediary
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may not act as or for an intermediary` intermediary IF
        "(d)" ... intermediary's `subject to a statutory disqualification as defined in section 3(a)(39) of the Exchange Act`
    AND NOT intermediary's `so permitted pursuant to Commission rule or order`


§§ `§ 227.501 Restrictions on resales`

-- AMBIGUITY "during the one-year period beginning when the securities were
-- issued". Does the period include its own anniversary? Reading (i): the
-- period runs from the issue date up to but not including the first
-- anniversary, so a transfer ON the anniversary is unrestricted (taken here —
-- a one-year period that began on day X has run when day X recurs). Reading
-- (ii): the anniversary is the last restricted day. The text does not say, and
-- the two readings differ on exactly one day per holding.

@ref § 227.501(a) — "the one-year period beginning when the securities were issued"; leap-safe by incrementing the YEAR
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A DATE
`the first anniversary of the issuance` transfer MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY   (transfer's `date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6)`))
         (DATE_MONTH (transfer's `date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6)`))
         (DATE_YEAR  (transfer's `date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6)`) PLUS `the resale restriction in years`)

@ref § 227.501(a)
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transfer falls within the one-year restricted period` transfer MEANS
    transfer's `date of the transfer` LESS THAN `the first anniversary of the issuance` transfer

@ref § 227.501(a)(1)-(4) — "unless such securities are transferred:"
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transfer falls within an exception in § 227.501(a)` transfer MEANS
        "unless such securities are transferred:"
    ..  "(1)" ... transfer's `to the issuer of the securities`
    ..  "(2)" ... transfer's `to an accredited investor`
    ..  "(3)" ... transfer's `as part of an offering registered with the Commission`
    ..  "(4)" ... transfer's `to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent, to a trust controlled by the purchaser, to a trust created for the benefit of such a family member, or in connection with the death or divorce of the purchaser or other similar circumstance`

@ref § 227.501(a)
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is permitted` transfer IF
        NOT `the transfer falls within the one-year restricted period` transfer
    OR  `the transfer falls within an exception in § 227.501(a)` transfer

-- § 227.501(b) is discharged by `the investor is an accredited investor` in
-- the annex above: it is § 230.501(a) plus the reasonable-belief limb, which
-- that predicate already carries.
--
-- § 227.501(c) is a pure definition carrier — thirteen relations plus adoptive
-- relationships, and the meaning of "spousal equivalent". No active node
-- carries its words, because the (a)(4) input field asserts membership rather
-- than enumerating it, so the words live here verbatim and nowhere else.
@ref § 227.501(c) — "member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent"` MEANS
        "includes a child, stepchild, grandchild, parent, stepparent, grandparent, spouse or spousal equivalent, sibling, mother-in-law, father-in-law, son-in-law, daughter-in-law, brother-in-law, or sister-in-law of the purchaser, and shall include adoptive relationships."
    ... "The term spousal equivalent means a cohabitant occupying a relationship generally equivalent to that of a spouse."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.504 Definition of "qualified purchaser"`

-- One sentence, and it is a definition rather than a test: every person to
-- whom securities are offered or sold under this part IS a qualified
-- purchaser for section 18(b)(3). The predicate is therefore constant TRUE on
-- its domain, which is the honest encoding and not a stub.
@ref § 227.504; 86 FR 3593 (Jan. 14, 2021), generally effective Mar. 15, 2021
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person to whom securities are offered or sold under this part is a qualified purchaser` IF
        "For purposes of section 18(b)(3) of the Securities Act [15 U.S.C. 77r(b)(3)], a \"qualified purchaser\" means any person to whom securities are offered or sold pursuant to an offering under §§ 227.100 through 227.504 (Regulation Crowdfunding)."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.100 Crowdfunding exemption and requirements`

-- The root of the part. Everything else either feeds this or is a duty that
-- arises once it is satisfied.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a)(1) — the issuer's twelve-month aggregate cap
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- F-CAP-12MONTH-ANCHOR lives here. The rule counts securities sold "during the
-- 12-month period preceding the date of such offer or sale"; CFI 100.05 and
-- intermediary FAQ 304.3 both say the window rolls from the date of EACH
-- CLOSING. The two readings are computed from two different inputs, side by
-- side, exactly so the choice is visible: reading A reads one number the
-- issuer supplies; reading B sums the closings whose twelve-month anniversary
-- has not yet passed.
--
-- AMBIGUITY "the aggregate amount of securities sold" — dollars, or a count of
-- securities? Reading (i): dollars (taken here, as everything else in the
-- section is dollars and $5,000,000 is a dollar figure). Reading (ii): a count
-- of securities (rejected as unworkable, but the words permit it).
--
-- AMBIGUITY the chapeau mixes tenses: "the aggregate amount of securities
-- SOLD ... including the securities OFFERED in such transaction". What is the
-- amount of "the securities offered in such transaction" for an offering that
-- has not closed? Reading (i): the maximum the issuer will accept where it
-- accepts oversubscriptions, and the target offering amount otherwise (taken
-- here, by parity with Instruction 1 to § 227.201(t), which says exactly that
-- for the neighbouring aggregation). Reading (ii): the target offering amount
-- always. Not resolved by § 227.100 itself.

@ref § 227.100(a)(1); F-CAP-12MONTH-ANCHOR reading B — CFI 100.05, intermediary FAQ 304.3
GIVEN issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing` issuer `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
    sum (map `the amount of the closing` (filter `the closing's twelve-month anniversary has not passed` (issuer's `closings in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`)))
    WHERE
        `the window opens` MEANS `the date that many years earlier` `the date of the offer or sale` 1
        `the closing's twelve-month anniversary has not passed` c MEANS c's `date` AT LEAST `the window opens`
        `the amount of the closing` c MEANS c's `amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`

@ref § 227.100(a)(1); F-CAP-12MONTH-ANCHOR
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount already sold in the twelve month window` interp issuer `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `twelve month window anchor`
    WHEN `rolling from each closing`          THEN `amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing` issuer `the date of the offer or sale`
    WHEN `from the date of such offer or sale` THEN issuer's `amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the 12-month period preceding the date of such offer or sale`

@ref § 227.100(a)(1) — "including the securities offered in such transaction"; cf § 227.201(t) Instruction 1
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount attributable to this transaction` offering MEANS
    IF   offering's `the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount`
    THEN offering's `maximum amount the issuer will accept`
    ELSE offering's `target offering amount`

@ref § 227.100(a)(1)
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap` interp issuer offering `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
          `the aggregate offering cap`
    MINUS `the amount already sold in the twelve month window` interp issuer `the date of the offer or sale`

@ref § 227.100(a)(1)
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(a)(1) — the aggregate amount does not exceed the cap` interp issuer offering `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
        "(1)" ... (      `the amount already sold in the twelve month window` interp issuer `the date of the offer or sale`
                   PLUS  `the amount attributable to this transaction` offering)
                  AT MOST `the aggregate offering cap`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a)(2) — the investor's twelve-month cap across all issuers
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Two forks meet here. F-ANNUAL-INCOME-PERIOD decides what "annual" means, and
-- F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL decides what an ENTITY investor's two quantities are —
-- the rule's own "annual income or net worth", or the revenue and net assets
-- CFI 100.02 substitutes. Note the consequence the register draws out: on the
-- staff's own two readings a natural person is measured on the calendar year
-- and an entity as of its most recent fiscal year end, so an encoding that
-- used one period for both would be wrong on one of them. This one does not.

@ref § 227.100(a)(2); F-ANNUAL-INCOME-PERIOD — CFI 100.06
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investor's annual income` interp investor MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `annual income period`
    WHEN `the calendar year`             THEN investor's `annual income for the calendar year`
    WHEN `the investor's own fiscal year` THEN investor's `annual income for the investor's own fiscal year`

@ref § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 1; F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL — CFI 100.02
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor MEANS
    IF   investor's `a natural person`
    THEN `the investor's annual income` interp investor
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `non-natural investor limit basis`
         WHEN `revenue or net assets`       THEN investor's `revenue for the most recent fiscal year`
         WHEN `annual income or net worth`  THEN `the investor's annual income` interp investor

@ref § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 1; F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL — CFI 100.02
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the second of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor MEANS
    IF   investor's `a natural person`
    THEN `the investor's net worth` investor
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `non-natural investor limit basis`
         WHEN `revenue or net assets`       THEN investor's `net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end`
         WHEN `annual income or net worth`  THEN `the investor's net worth` investor

@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(i)-(ii) — "the greater of the investor's annual income or net worth"
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor MEANS
    max (`the first of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor)
        (`the second of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor)

@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(ii) — "if both the investor's annual income and net worth are equal to or more than $124,000"
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both measured quantities are at or above the tier boundary` interp investor MEANS
        `the first of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor  AT LEAST `the investor tier boundary`
    AND `the second of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor AT LEAST `the investor tier boundary`

@ref § 227.100(a)(2)(i)-(ii) — the two exhaustive tiers
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investment limit for the investor` interp investor MEANS
    BRANCH IF `both measured quantities are at or above the tier boundary` interp investor
           THEN min (`the greater of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor TIMES `the upper investment limit rate percent` DIVIDED BY 100)
                    `the investor ceiling`
           OTHERWISE max `the investor floor`
                         (`the greater of the investor's two measured quantities` interp investor TIMES `the lower investment limit rate percent` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- AMBIGUITY Instruction 2 to paragraph (a)(2): "A person's annual income and
-- net worth may be calculated jointly with that person's spouse; however, when
-- such a joint calculation is used, the aggregate investment of the investor
-- spouses may not exceed the limit that would apply to an individual investor
-- at that income or net worth level." Reading (i): ONE shared limit for the
-- couple, tested against their combined investments (taken here — "the
-- aggregate investment of the investor spouses may not exceed the limit"
-- says so in terms). Reading (ii): the joint figures lift the couple into the
-- higher tier while each spouse retains a full individual limit (rejected —
-- it reads "aggregate" out of the sentence, but it is the reading a
-- portal's per-investor form silently implements). The two disagree on every
-- married pair using the joint calculation.
@ref § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 2 — the joint spousal calculation
GIVEN investor IS AN InvestorProfile
      `this investment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount tested against the investor's limit` investor `this investment` MEANS
    IF   investor's `annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse`
    THEN investor's `the aggregate investment of the investor spouses` PLUS `this investment`
    ELSE investor's `aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months` PLUS `this investment`

@ref § 227.100(a)(2) — "Where the purchaser is not an accredited investor ... shall not exceed"
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
      `this investment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded` interp investor `this investment` MEANS
        "(2)" ... `the investor is an accredited investor` investor
    ..  `the amount tested against the investor's limit` investor `this investment` AT MOST `the investment limit for the investor` interp investor

-- Instruction 3 to paragraph (a)(2) is a SAFE HARBOUR, not a limb: the issuer
-- may rely on the intermediary's § 227.303(b) efforts "provided that the
-- issuer does not know" the limits are or would be exceeded. It rests on the
-- issuer's knowledge, which is a fact and not another rule's outcome, so it
-- does not make § 227.100 depend on § 227.303.
@ref § 227.100(a)(2) Instruction 3
GIVEN interp    IS AN Interpretation
      investor  IS AN InvestorProfile
      offering  IS AN OfferingProfile
      `this investment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(a)(2) — satisfied, or within the intermediary-reliance safe harbour` interp investor offering `this investment` MEANS
        `100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded` interp investor `this investment`
    OR  NOT offering's `the issuer knows that the investor has exceeded, or would exceed, the investor limits`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a)(3) — one compliant intermediary, exclusively
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref Instruction to § 227.100(a)(3); F-ONE-INTERMEDIARY-SCOPE — CFI 100.03
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`more than one intermediary has been used` interp offering MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `one intermediary scope`
    WHEN `the prohibition binds the offering` THEN offering's `more than one intermediary used in this offering`
    WHEN `the prohibition binds the issuer`   THEN offering's `more than one intermediary used by the issuer for this capital raise`

@ref § 227.100(a)(3) and the Instruction thereto
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(a)(3) — conducted through one compliant intermediary, exclusively` interp offering MEANS
        "(3)" ... offering's `conducted through an intermediary that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`
    AND offering's `conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform`
    AND NOT `more than one intermediary has been used` interp offering

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a)(4) — compliance with section 4A(b), with a carve-out
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref § 227.100(a)(4) and its proviso
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(a)(4) — the issuer complies with section 4A(b)` offering MEANS
        "(4)" ... offering's `the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`
    ..  offering's `the only failure to comply is with §§ 227.202, 227.203(a)(3) and 227.203(b)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (b) — applicability: the six issuer ineligibility limbs
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref § 227.100(b)(2); F-REPORTING-DISQUALIFICATION — CFI 100.04
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is caught by the Exchange Act reporting limb` interp issuer MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `reporting disqualification tense`
    WHEN `presently subject to the reporting requirement`
         THEN issuer's `subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`
    WHEN `ever subject to the reporting requirement`
         THEN      issuer's `subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`
              OR   issuer's `formerly subject to section 13 or 15(d) reporting, since terminated or suspended`

@ref § 227.100(b)(5) and the Instruction thereto
GIVEN issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is delinquent in its ongoing reports` issuer MEANS
        issuer's `has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`
    AND NOT issuer's `has filed with the Commission and provided to investors the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement`

-- § 227.100(b)(7) is [Reserved]. It is a deliberate labelled STUB rather than
-- a silent gap: between 2021-01-14 and 2023-03-01 the paragraph carried the
-- COVID-era expedited offering route added by 86 FR 3590 with a built-in
-- sunset, and on 2023-03-01 it reverted to "[Reserved]". THE WORDS OF THAT
-- TEXT ARE NOT IN THE BUNDLE — P1 captured only the text in force from
-- 2023-03-01 — so the stub carries the provenance and NOT the words. Inventing
-- them from memory would be fabrication, which is the one thing a corpus
-- cannot recover from.
@ref § 227.100(b)(7) [Reserved]; added 86 FR 3590 (Jan. 14, 2021), lapsed 2023-03-01
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`100(b)(7) — reserved` MEANS
        "(7) [Reserved]"
    ... "[the paragraph carried a COVID-era expedited offering route from 2021-01-14 until it lapsed on 2023-03-01; that text is not in this bundle and is deliberately not reproduced]"
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.100(b)(1)-(6)
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer` interp issuer IF
        "(1)" ... NOT issuer's `organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia`
    ..  "(2)" ... `the issuer is caught by the Exchange Act reporting limb` interp issuer
    ..  "(3)" ... issuer's `an investment company as defined in section 3 of the Investment Company Act, or excluded from that definition by section 3(b) or section 3(c) of that Act`
    ..  "(4)" ... `no exemption is available because of a disqualification` issuer
    ..  "(5)" ... `the issuer is delinquent in its ongoing reports` issuer
    ..  "(6)" ... issuer's `no specific business plan, or a business plan to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (c), (d), (e) — the three definitional paragraphs
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (c) is SCOPED: the extended meaning of "issuer" reaches four named places
-- and nowhere else. That scoping is the operative content, and no active node
-- restates it, so the words live here.
@ref § 227.100(c) and the Instruction thereto
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the extended meaning of "issuer" in § 227.100(c)` MEANS
        "For purposes of § 227.201(r), calculating aggregate amounts offered and sold in § 227.100(a) and § 227.201(t), and determining whether an issuer has previously sold securities in § 227.201(t)(3), issuer includes all entities controlled by or under common control with the issuer and any predecessors of the issuer."
    ... "The term control means the possession, direct or indirect, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of the entity, whether through the ownership of voting securities, by contract or otherwise."
    ... TRUE

-- (d) has two halves. The first — "investor means any investor or any
-- potential investor, as the context requires" — is a definition that DEFERS
-- TO CONTEXT and so cannot be resolved by a type; it is carried inert. The
-- second is computable, and it is what collides with § 227.202(b)(2) at fork
-- F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD.
@ref § 227.100(d) first sentence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "investor" in § 227.100(d)` MEANS
        "For purposes of this part, investor means any investor or any potential investor, as the context requires."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.100(d) second sentence; 17 CFR § 270.3a-9
GIVEN vehicle IS A `Crowdfunding vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crowdfunding vehicle is not considered an investor for the purposes of this part` vehicle IF
    `the vehicle is a crowdfunding vehicle deemed not to be an investment company` vehicle

-- (e) is a bare outward pointer to § 230.152, which the bundle does not carry.
-- It is reproduced and not expanded.
@ref § 227.100(e)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`integration with other offerings` MEANS
        "To determine whether offers and sales should be integrated, see § 230.152 of this chapter."
    ... TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a) — the exemption itself
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref § 227.100(a) chapeau with (a)(1)-(4) and (b)
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile
      `this investment` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crowdfunding exemption is available` interp issuer offering investor `this investment` `the date of the offer or sale` IF
        "(a) An issuer may offer or sell securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act, provided that:"
    ... `100(a)(1) — the aggregate amount does not exceed the cap` interp issuer offering `the date of the offer or sale`
    ... `100(a)(2) — satisfied, or within the intermediary-reliance safe harbour` interp investor offering `this investment`
    ... `100(a)(3) — conducted through one compliant intermediary, exclusively` interp offering
    ... `100(a)(4) — the issuer complies with section 4A(b)` offering
    ... NOT `the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer` interp issuer


§§ `The regulative vocabulary — who acts, and what the acts are`

-- Every duty, permission and prohibition in this part falls on one of five
-- parties, and every one of them is an act that can be observed to have
-- happened or not happened by a deadline. Both are declared once here so the
-- regulative rules below read as the regulation reads.

@ref the parties of 17 CFR part 227
DECLARE `Reg CF party` IS ONE OF
    `the issuer`
    `the intermediary`
    `the funding portal`
    `the investor`
    `the qualified third party`

@ref the acts required, permitted or prohibited by 17 CFR part 227
DECLARE `Reg CF act` IS ONE OF
    -- Subpart B, the issuer's acts.
    `file with the Commission and provide to investors and the relevant intermediary the information required by § 227.201`
    `file with the Commission and post on the issuer's Web site an annual report`
    `file a Form C offering statement`
    `file a Form C/A amendment to the offering statement`
    `file a Form C-U progress update`
    `file a final Form C-U disclosing the total amount of securities sold`
    `file a Form C-AR annual report`
    `file a Form C-AR/A amendment to the annual report`
    `file a Form C-TR termination of reporting`
    `advertise the terms of the offering`
    `communicate with investors through the intermediary's communication channels`
    `compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings`
    `solicit or accept money, other consideration, or a commitment`
    `communicate to determine whether there is any interest in a contemplated securities offering`
    -- Subpart C, the intermediary's acts.
    `deny access to its platform to the issuer`
    `remove the offering from its platform, cancel the offering, and return the funds committed by investors`
    `accept an investment commitment`
    `deliver the educational materials to the investor`
    `make the issuer information publicly available on its platform`
    `give or send the investor notice of the investment commitment`
    `give or send the investor notice of the material change`
    `give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount`
    `direct the refund of investor funds`
    `prevent investors from making investment commitments with respect to that offering`
    `direct the qualified third party to transmit the funds to the issuer`
    `give or send the investor confirmation of the transaction`
    `compensate a person for the personally identifiable information of an investor`
    -- Subpart C, the investor's act.
    `reconfirm the investment commitment`
    `cancel the investment commitment`
    -- Subpart D, the funding portal's acts.
    `register on Form Funding Portal and become a member of a national securities association`
    `file an amendment to Form Funding Portal`
    `file a withdrawal of registration on Form Funding Portal`
    `re-certify on Schedule C to Form Funding Portal`
    `make and preserve the records required by § 227.404`
    `permit the examination and inspection of its business and business operations`


§§ `§ 227.201 Disclosure requirements`

-- ENCODED BEFORE §§ 227.202 and 227.203 for the reason given at § 227.503:
-- § 227.202(a) CALLS § 227.201 ("must include the disclosure required by
-- paragraphs (a), (b), (c) ... of § 227.201"), while § 227.201(x) merely asks
-- whether the issuer previously COMPLIED with § 227.202 — which is a fact, and
-- so an input field. Outcome-references are calls; compliance-references are
-- facts. The same distinction orders § 227.201 before § 227.203.
--
-- AMBIGUITY the chapeau: "must file with the Commission AND provide to
-- investors AND the relevant intermediary the following information". Is that
-- one duty with three recipients, three parallel duties, or a single duty
-- whose content is the list? Reading (i): one duty whose content is the
-- completeness predicate below, with the three recipients named inside the act
-- (taken here — it keeps the twenty-six items in one place an engine can
-- execute, and the party and deadline in one place a process diagram can
-- draw). Reading (ii): twenty-six separate obligations, one per lettered
-- paragraph, which is what the plural "the following information" most
-- literally licenses. This is an ENCODING-PLACEMENT choice, not a reading of
-- the words, and it is registered as one.

@ref § 227.201(a)-(z) — the completeness of the disclosure
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offering statement discloses the information required by § 227.201` offering IF
        "(a)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the name, legal status, physical address and Web site of the issuer`
    ... "(b)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the names of the directors and officers, their positions, tenure and business experience during the past three years`
    ... "(c)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the name of each beneficial owner of twenty percent or more of the issuer's outstanding voting equity securities`
    ... "(d)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the business of the issuer and the anticipated business plan of the issuer`
    ... "(e)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the current number of employees of the issuer`
    ... "(f)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a discussion of the material factors that make an investment in the issuer speculative or risky`
    ... "(g)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the target offering amount and the deadline to reach the target offering amount`
    ... "(h)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `whether the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount and how oversubscriptions will be allocated`
    ... "(i)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the purpose and intended use of the offering proceeds`
    ... "(j)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the process to complete the transaction or cancel an investment commitment`
    ... "(k)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a statement that an investor who does not reconfirm after a material change will have the commitment cancelled and the funds returned`
    ... "(l)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the price to the public of the securities or the method for determining the price`
    ... "(m)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer`
    ... "(n)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the name, SEC file number and CRD number of the intermediary`
    ... "(o)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the intermediary's financial interests in the issuer's transaction and in the issuer`
    ... "(p)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer`
    ... "(q)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years`
    ... "(r)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold`
    ... "(s)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a discussion of the issuer's financial condition`
    ... "(t)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the financial statements and tax information required by paragraph (t)`
    ... "(u)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `any matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016`
    ... "(v)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount`
    ... "(w)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `where on the issuer's Web site investors will be able to find the issuer's annual report, and by when`
    ... "(x)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202`
    ... "(y)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `any material information necessary to make the statements made not misleading`
    ... "(z)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `any written communication or broadcast script provided in accordance with § 227.206 or § 230.241`

-- (aa) is [Reserved], and is a labelled stub for the same reason § 227.100(b)(7)
-- is: an in-order corpus should have no silent gap, and the words that once
-- stood there (§ 227.201(bb) is the neighbouring casualty) are not in the
-- bundle.
@ref § 227.201(aa) [Reserved]
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`201(aa) — reserved` MEANS
        "(aa) [Reserved]"
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.201 Instruction — cross-references satisfy the section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction to § 227.201 on cross-references` MEANS
        "If disclosure provided pursuant to any paragraph of this section also satisfies the requirements of one or more other paragraphs of this section, it is not necessary to repeat the disclosure. Instead of repeating information, an issuer may include a cross-reference to disclosure contained elsewhere in the offering statement or report, including to information in the financial statements."
    ... TRUE

-- --- § 227.201(t) — the financial-statement tier ---------------------------
--
-- The cleanest numeric decision in the part, and the one most likely to be
-- encoded WRONG, because paragraph (t)(3) inverts its own main clause: "More
-- than $618,000, financial statements ... audited ...; provided, however, that
-- for issuers that have not previously sold securities in reliance on section
-- 4(a)(6), offerings that have a target offering amount of more than $618,000,
-- but not more than $1,235,000, financial statements ... reviewed ...". A
-- BRANCH written in citation order returns "audited" for a first-time issuer
-- at $1,000,000 and is wrong. The proviso is therefore tested BEFORE the
-- general limb, which is why the arms below are not in the source's order.
--
-- AMBIGUITY "issuers that have not previously sold securities in reliance on
-- section 4(a)(6)" — previously EVER, or previously within the twelve-month
-- aggregation window? Reading (i): ever (taken here — the phrase carries no
-- window, and § 227.100(c) tells us WHO counts for this test, which would be
-- odd if it also carried a WHEN). Reading (ii): within the same twelve months
-- the paragraph otherwise aggregates over. Not resolved by the text.

@ref § 227.201(t)(1)-(3)
DECLARE `financial statement requirement` IS ONE OF
    `tax return information with financial statements certified by the principal executive officer`
    `financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`
    `financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`

@ref § 227.201(t) chapeau with Instruction 1 thereto
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t)` interp issuer offering MEANS
          `the amount already sold in the twelve month window` interp issuer (issuer's `date the offering statement was filed`)
    PLUS  `the amount attributable to this transaction` offering

@ref § 227.201(t)(1)-(3); the (t)(3) proviso is tested before the (t)(3) main clause
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A `financial statement requirement`
DECIDE `the financial statements required` interp issuer offering IS
    BRANCH IF `the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t)` interp issuer offering AT MOST `the tax return information ceiling`
           THEN `tax return information with financial statements certified by the principal executive officer`
           IF `the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t)` interp issuer offering AT MOST `the reviewed statements ceiling`
           THEN `financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`
           IF     NOT issuer's `previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`
              AND `the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t)` interp issuer offering AT MOST `the first-time issuer reviewed ceiling`
           THEN `financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`
           OTHERWISE `financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`

-- Instruction 2 to paragraph (t) — voluntary uplift. A permission, and one
-- that no fact can falsify, so it is carried as a definition rather than
-- turned into a test that would always return TRUE.
@ref § 227.201(t) Instruction 2
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an issuer may voluntarily meet the requirements for a higher aggregate target offering amount` MEANS
        "An issuer may voluntarily meet the requirements of this paragraph (t) for a higher aggregate target offering amount."
    ... TRUE

-- Instruction 4 to paragraph (t) — the 120-day staleness roll. This is the ONE
-- place in the part where a holiday is mentioned, and the roll below skips
-- weekends only; see the business-days note above.
@ref § 227.201(t) Instruction 4
GIVEN `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the hundred and twentieth day, rolled off a weekend` `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year` MEANS
    `rolled forward off a weekend`
        (Date (Day `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year` PLUS `the financial statement staleness window in days`))

@ref § 227.201(t) Instruction 4 — financial statements may be for the two years prior in the first 120 days
GIVEN `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year` IS A DATE
      `the date of the offering`                           IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offering is conducted in the first 120 days of the fiscal year` `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year` `the date of the offering` MEANS
    `the date of the offering` AT MOST `the hundred and twentieth day, rolled off a weekend` `the end of the most recently completed fiscal year`

-- --- § 227.201(u) — pre-2016 disqualifying matters -------------------------

@ref § 227.201(u) and the Instruction thereto
GIVEN issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the failure to disclose a pre-2016 matter does not defeat the exemption` issuer IF
        issuer's `matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016`
    AND NOT issuer's `those matters disclosed`
    AND issuer's `did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known of the existence of the undisclosed matter`

-- --- the duty ---------------------------------------------------------------

@ref § 227.201 chapeau
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's § 227.201 disclosure duty` offering MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    MUST  `file with the Commission and provide to investors and the relevant intermediary the information required by § 227.201`
          PROVIDED `the offering statement discloses the information required by § 227.201` offering
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.201: the offering statement does not disclose everything the section requires"


§§ `§ 227.202 Ongoing reporting requirements`

-- The annual report's CONTENT is § 227.201's, by reference — Instruction 1 to
-- paragraph (a) even re-applies five of § 227.201(t)'s instructions — which is
-- the call that puts § 227.201 first.

@ref § 227.202(a) — the eleven § 227.201 paragraphs the annual report must carry
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual report carries the disclosure § 227.202(a) requires` offering IF
        "(a)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the name, legal status, physical address and Web site of the issuer`
    ... "(b)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the names of the directors and officers, their positions, tenure and business experience during the past three years`
    ... "(c)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the name of each beneficial owner of twenty percent or more of the issuer's outstanding voting equity securities`
    ... "(d)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the business of the issuer and the anticipated business plan of the issuer`
    ... "(e)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `the current number of employees of the issuer`
    ... "(f)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a discussion of the material factors that make an investment in the issuer speculative or risky`
    ... "(m)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer`
    ... "(p)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer`
    ... "(q)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years`
    ... "(r)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold`
    ... "(x)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202`
    ... "(s)" ... offering's `the disclosure provided`'s `a discussion of the issuer's financial condition`

@ref § 227.202(a) — "no later than 120 days after the end of the fiscal year covered by the report"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's annual report duty` offering MEANS
    PARTY  `the issuer`
    MUST   `file with the Commission and post on the issuer's Web site an annual report`
           PROVIDED `the annual report carries the disclosure § 227.202(a) requires` offering
    WITHIN `the annual report deadline in days`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.202(a): the annual report was not filed within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year, or does not carry the required disclosure"

-- --- § 227.202(b) — the five events that end the duty ----------------------
--
-- F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD lives in limb (2). The register calls it the most
-- interesting fork it produced, because the two readings do not merely differ,
-- they pull against two different provisions of the SAME part: § 227.100(d)
-- says a crowdfunding vehicle "is not considered an investor for the purposes
-- of this part", which makes the vehicle one holder; CFI 202.02 looks THROUGH
-- the vehicle to the people behind it for this one count. An encoding that
-- picked either silently would have decided that tension without saying so.

@ref § 227.202(b)(2); F-HOLDERS-OF-RECORD — CFI 202.02 against § 227.100(d)
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the count of record holders for § 227.202(b)(2)` interp issuer MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `holders of record basis`
    WHEN `the investors who invested in the offering` THEN issuer's `investors who invested in the offering`
    WHEN `the register of holders of record`          THEN issuer's `holders of record`

@ref § 227.202(b)(1)-(5)
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting` interp issuer IF
        "(1)" ... issuer's `required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`
    ..  "(2)" ... (    issuer's `annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part` AT LEAST 1
                   AND `the count of record holders for § 227.202(b)(2)` interp issuer LESS THAN `the holders of record threshold`)
    ..  "(3)" ... (    issuer's `annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part` AT LEAST 3
                   AND issuer's `total assets` AT MOST `the total assets ceiling ending ongoing reporting`)
    ..  "(4)" ... issuer's `all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6) repurchased, including any payment in full of debt securities or any complete redemption of redeemable securities`
    ..  "(5)" ... issuer's `liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law`

-- AMBIGUITY does the ongoing reporting duty END when a paragraph (b) event
-- occurs, or only when Form C-TR is filed? § 227.203(b)(3) gives the issuer
-- five business days "from the date on which the issuer becomes eligible to
-- terminate its reporting obligation" to file the C-TR, which implies the two
-- are different moments. Reading (i): eligibility ends the duty and the C-TR
-- is a notice of that fact (taken here — § 227.202(b) says "must continue to
-- comply ... until one of the following occurs", and the C-TR is not one of
-- the five). Reading (ii): the duty continues until the C-TR is filed, so a
-- late C-TR extends the reporting obligation. Not resolved by the text.


§§ `§ 227.203 Filing requirements and form`

@ref § 227.203(a)(1) — "prior to the commencement of the offering of securities"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's offering statement filing duty` offering MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    MUST  `file a Form C offering statement`
          PROVIDED     offering's `the offering statement filed prior to the commencement of the offering`
                   AND `the offering statement discloses the information required by § 227.201` offering
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(a)(1): Form C was not filed prior to the commencement of the offering, or does not include the information required by § 227.201"

@ref § 227.203(a)(2) — material changes, and the reconfirmation box
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's offering statement amendment duty` offering MEANS
    IF   offering's `a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer`
    THEN PARTY `the issuer`
         MUST  `file a Form C/A amendment to the offering statement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(a)(2): no Form C/A was filed to disclose a material change"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- § 227.203(a)(3)(iii) is a GATE on an obligation, not an obligation: where
-- the intermediary posts frequent progress updates, (i) and (ii) fall away —
-- but the FINAL Form C-U survives the disapplication in terms ("however, the
-- issuer must still file a Form C-U ... no later than five business days after
-- the offering deadline"). That asymmetry is the whole content of the limb.
@ref § 227.203(a)(3)(i) and (iii)
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's progress update duty` intermediary MEANS
    IF   "(iii)" ... intermediary's `makes publicly available on its platform frequent updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY  `the issuer`
         MUST   `file a Form C-U progress update`
         WITHIN `five business days`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(a)(3)(i): no Form C-U was filed within five business days of reaching 50 percent or 100 percent of the target offering amount"

@ref § 227.203(a)(3)(ii) and (iii) — the final Form C-U survives the disapplication
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's final progress update duty` offering MEANS
    IF   offering's `the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount`
    THEN PARTY  `the issuer`
         MUST   `file a final Form C-U disclosing the total amount of securities sold`
         WITHIN `five business days`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(a)(3)(ii): no final Form C-U was filed within five business days after the offering deadline"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref § 227.203(a)(3) Instruction — consolidation of Forms C-U triggered in one five-day window
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction on consolidating progress updates` MEANS
        "If multiple Forms C-U are triggered within the same five business day period, the issuer may consolidate such progress updates into one Form C-U, so long as the Form C-U discloses the most recent threshold that was met and the Form C-U is filed with the Commission and provided to investors and the relevant intermediary by the day on which the first progress update is due."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.203(b)(1) — "no later than 120 days after the end of the fiscal year covered by the report"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's Form C-AR duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `the issuer`
    MUST   `file a Form C-AR annual report`
    WITHIN `the annual report deadline in days`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(b)(1): Form C-AR was not filed within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year"

-- AMBIGUITY § 227.203(b)(2) requires the C-AR/A "as soon as practicable after
-- discovery of the need for the material change". "As soon as practicable" is
-- vague with no competing parse: there is one reading, and its boundary is
-- undecidable on the facts of any particular case. It is encoded as a deadline
-- the fact-supplier must resolve — the WITHIN below carries five business days
-- BY ANALOGY to the neighbouring paragraphs, and that analogy is an encoding
-- choice, not the text.
@ref § 227.203(b)(2) — "as soon as practicable after discovery of the need for the material change"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's Form C-AR amendment duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `the issuer`
    MUST   `file a Form C-AR/A amendment to the annual report`
    WITHIN `five business days`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(b)(2): no Form C-AR/A was filed as soon as practicable after discovery of the need for a material change"

@ref § 227.203(b)(3) — "within five business days from the date on which the issuer becomes eligible"
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's termination of reporting duty` interp issuer MEANS
    IF   `the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting` interp issuer
    THEN PARTY  `the issuer`
         MUST   `file a Form C-TR termination of reporting`
         WITHIN `five business days`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.203(b)(3): Form C-TR was not filed within five business days of becoming eligible to terminate the reporting obligation"
    ELSE FULFILLED


§§ `§ 227.206 Solicitations of interest and other communications`

-- ENCODED BEFORE § 227.204 because § 227.204(a)(1) EXCEPTS it: "except for
-- oral or written communications that meet the requirements of paragraph (b)
-- of this section or of § 227.206". The exception is a call on § 227.206's
-- outcome, so § 227.206 comes first. § 227.206 was added by 86 FR 3592 and did
-- not exist before 2021-03-15; no dated arm is written for that, because the
-- arm would sit below this module's encoding floor and be dead.

@ref § 227.206(b)(1)-(3) — the three statements the communication must contain
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires` communication IF
        "(1)" ... communication's `states that no money or other consideration is being solicited, and if sent in response, will not be accepted`
    ... "(2)" ... communication's `states that no offer to buy the securities can be accepted and no part of the purchase price can be received until the offering statement is filed and only through an intermediary's platform`
    ... "(3)" ... communication's `states that a person's indication of interest involves no obligation or commitment of any kind`

@ref § 227.206(a) first sentence — the permission
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's permission to solicit interest before filing` communication MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    MAY   `communicate to determine whether there is any interest in a contemplated securities offering`
          PROVIDED     communication's `made before the filing of the offering statement`
                   AND `the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires` communication
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

@ref § 227.206(a) last sentence — "No solicitation or acceptance of money or other consideration ... is permitted until the offering statement is filed"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer must not take money before the offering statement is filed` MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    SHANT `solicit or accept money, other consideration, or a commitment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.206(a): money, other consideration or a commitment was solicited or accepted before the offering statement was filed"

@ref § 227.206(a) second sentence; § 227.206(c)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the character and permitted response content of a solicitation of interest` MEANS
        "Such communications are deemed to be an offer of a security for sale for purposes of the antifraud provisions of the Federal securities laws."
    ... "This issuer may require the name, address, telephone number, and/or email address in any response form included pursuant to this paragraph (c)."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.204 Advertising`

-- § 227.204(b)(1)-(3) is a CLOSED PERMITTED-CONTENT LIST that the active node
-- reaches only by cross-reference — the record field is worded "includes no
-- more than the information specified in § 227.204(b)(1) through (3)", which
-- asserts membership rather than enumerating it. Under the enumeration-label
-- ruling that is one of the two cases where a verbatim quotation survives:
-- these words live here and nowhere else in the module.
@ref § 227.204(b)(1)-(3) — the closed permitted-content list
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the information a notice may contain under § 227.204(b)` MEANS
        "(1) A statement that the issuer is conducting an offering pursuant to section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act, the name of the intermediary through which the offering is being conducted, and information (including a link in any written communications) directing the potential investor to the intermediary's platform;"
    ... "(2) The terms of the offering; and"
    ... "(3) Factual information about the legal identity and business location of the issuer, limited to the name of the issuer of the security, the address, phone number and Web site of the issuer, the email address of a representative of the issuer and a brief description of the business of the issuer."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.204(b) — when a notice may advertise the terms of the offering
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b)` communication IF
        communication's `directs investors to the intermediary's platform`
    AND communication's `includes no more than the information specified in § 227.204(b)(1) through (3)`

@ref § 227.204(a)(1) — the prohibition and its two exceptions
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer must not advertise the terms of the offering` communication MEANS
    IF       `the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b)` communication
         OR  `the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires` communication
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the issuer`
         SHANT `advertise the terms of the offering`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.204(a)(1): the terms of the offering were advertised otherwise than by a notice meeting § 227.204(b) or a communication meeting § 227.206"

@ref § 227.204(a)(2) Instruction — "issuer includes persons acting on behalf of the issuer"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "issuer" in § 227.204(a)` MEANS
        "For purposes of this paragraph (a), issuer includes persons acting on behalf of the issuer."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.204(c) — communication through the intermediary's channels, with identification
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's permission to use the intermediary's communication channels` communication MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    MAY   `communicate with investors through the intermediary's communication channels`
          PROVIDED     communication's `made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform`
                   AND communication's `the issuer identifies itself as the issuer in the communication`
                   AND communication's `a person acting on behalf of the issuer identifies that affiliation in the communication`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

@ref § 227.204(d) — the concurrent-offering disclosure-document safe harbour
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the concurrent-offering safe harbour in § 227.204(d)` MEANS
        "an issuer conducting an offering in reliance on Regulation Crowdfunding concurrently with another offering that discloses the terms of the Regulation Crowdfunding offering in the disclosure document for the other offering will not be deemed to have exceeded these disclosure limitations if the disclosure document for the other offering satisfies all the other requirements of this section."
    ... "If the disclosure document for the other offering is filed on the Commission's Electronic Data Gathering and Retrieval System (EDGAR), the link required by paragraph (b)(1) may not be a live hyperlink."
    ... TRUE

-- § 227.204(e) is a PURE DEFINITION CARRIER: six named items, referenced by
-- every other advertising provision and enumerated nowhere else. Its node is
-- literally TRUE, and that is the point — the words are the content.
@ref § 227.204(e) Instruction — "terms of the offering"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "terms of the offering"` MEANS
        "For purposes of this section, terms of the offering means the amount of securities offered, the nature of the securities, the price of the securities, the closing date of the offering period, the planned use of proceeds and the issuer's progress toward meeting its funding target."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.205 Promoter compensation`

-- (a) is a conditional PERMISSION and (b) is the residual PROHIBITION, and (b)
-- is drafted by reference to (a) and to § 227.204 — which is why § 227.205
-- comes after both.

@ref § 227.205(a) and the Instruction thereto
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer's permission to compensate a promoter` communication MEANS
    PARTY `the issuer`
    MAY   `compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings`
          PROVIDED     communication's `made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform`
                   AND communication's `clearly discloses the receipt, past or prospective, of compensation with the communication`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

@ref § 227.205(b) — "Other than as set forth in paragraph (a) of this section"
GIVEN communication IS A Communication
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the issuer must not otherwise compensate a promoter` communication MEANS
    IF       (    communication's `made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform`
              AND communication's `clearly discloses the receipt, past or prospective, of compensation with the communication`)
         OR  `the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b)` communication
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the issuer`
         SHANT `compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the issuer` BECAUSE "§ 227.205(b): a promoter was compensated otherwise than under § 227.205(a) or by a notice permitted by § 227.204"


§§ `§ 227.300 Intermediaries`

@ref § 227.300(a)(1)-(2) — the status test
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person qualifies to act as an intermediary` intermediary IF
        "(1)" ... (    intermediary's `registered with the Commission as a broker under section 15(b) of the Exchange Act`
                   OR  intermediary's `registered as a funding portal in accordance with § 227.400`)
    ... "(2)" ... intermediary's `a member of a national securities association registered under section 15A of the Exchange Act`

@ref § 227.300(b)(1)-(2) — the intermediary's own financial interest
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the intermediary's financial interest is permitted` intermediary MEANS
        "(1)" ... intermediary's `that financial interest received from the issuer as compensation for the services provided in connection with the offer or sale`
    ... "(2)" ... intermediary's `that financial interest consists of securities of the same class and having the same terms, conditions and rights as the securities being offered`

@ref § 227.300(b) — the flat prohibition on a director, officer or partner holding a financial interest
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary's financial interests comply with § 227.300(b)` intermediary IF
        NOT intermediary's `a director, officer or partner of the intermediary has a financial interest in the issuer`
    AND (    NOT intermediary's `the intermediary has a financial interest in the issuer`
         OR  `the intermediary's financial interest is permitted` intermediary)

@ref § 227.300(c)(2)(i)-(iv) — the four negative limbs of "funding portal"
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary is a funding portal` intermediary IF
        NOT "(i)"   ... intermediary's `offers investment advice or recommendations`
    AND NOT "(ii)"  ... intermediary's `solicits purchases, sales or offers to buy the securities displayed on its platform`
    AND NOT "(iii)" ... intermediary's `compensates employees, agents, or other persons for such solicitation or based on the sale of securities displayed or referenced on its platform`
    AND NOT "(iv)"  ... intermediary's `holds, manages, possesses, or otherwise handles investor funds or securities`

@ref § 227.300(c)(1), (3), (4) and the Instruction to paragraph (c)(4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definitions in § 227.300(c)` MEANS
        "(1) Associated person of a funding portal or person associated with a funding portal means any partner, officer, director or manager of a funding portal (or any person occupying a similar status or performing similar functions), any person directly or indirectly controlling or controlled by such funding portal, or any employee of a funding portal, except that any person associated with a funding portal whose functions are solely clerical or ministerial shall not be included in the meaning of such term for purposes of section 15(b) of the Exchange Act (other than paragraphs (4) and (6) of section 15(b) of the Exchange Act)."
    ... "(3) Intermediary means a broker registered under section 15(b) of the Exchange Act or a funding portal registered under § 227.400 and includes, where relevant, an associated person of the registered broker or registered funding portal."
    ... "(4) Platform means a program or application accessible via the Internet or other similar electronic communication medium through which a registered broker or a registered funding portal acts as an intermediary in a transaction involving the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act."
    ... "An intermediary through which a crowdfunding transaction is conducted may engage in back office or other administrative functions other than on the intermediary's platform."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.302 Account opening`

@ref § 227.302(b)(1)(i)-(ix) — the nine educational-material items
DECLARE `Educational materials` HAS
    `the process for the offer, purchase and issuance of securities through the intermediary and the risks associated with purchasing securities under section 4(a)(6)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the types of securities available for purchase on the platform and the risks associated with each type, including the risk of having limited voting power as a result of dilution`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restrictions on the resale of a security offered and sold under section 4(a)(6)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the types of information an issuer is required to provide under § 227.202, the frequency of delivery and the possibility that those obligations may terminate`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the limitations on the amounts an investor may invest pursuant to § 227.100(a)(2)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the limitations on an investor's right to cancel an investment commitment and the circumstances in which a commitment may be cancelled by the issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the need for the investor to consider whether investing in such a security is appropriate for that investor`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `that following completion of an offering there may or may not be any ongoing relationship between the issuer and intermediary`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `that under certain circumstances an issuer may cease to publish annual reports and an investor may not continually have current financial information`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `explained in plain language and otherwise designed to communicate effectively and accurately`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref § 227.302(b)(1)(i)-(ix)
GIVEN materials IS AN `Educational materials`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the educational materials carry everything § 227.302(b)(1) requires` materials IF
        "(i)"    ... materials's `the process for the offer, purchase and issuance of securities through the intermediary and the risks associated with purchasing securities under section 4(a)(6)`
    ... "(ii)"   ... materials's `the types of securities available for purchase on the platform and the risks associated with each type, including the risk of having limited voting power as a result of dilution`
    ... "(iii)"  ... materials's `the restrictions on the resale of a security offered and sold under section 4(a)(6)`
    ... "(iv)"   ... materials's `the types of information an issuer is required to provide under § 227.202, the frequency of delivery and the possibility that those obligations may terminate`
    ... "(v)"    ... materials's `the limitations on the amounts an investor may invest pursuant to § 227.100(a)(2)`
    ... "(vi)"   ... materials's `the limitations on an investor's right to cancel an investment commitment and the circumstances in which a commitment may be cancelled by the issuer`
    ... "(vii)"  ... materials's `the need for the investor to consider whether investing in such a security is appropriate for that investor`
    ... "(viii)" ... materials's `that following completion of an offering there may or may not be any ongoing relationship between the issuer and intermediary`
    ... "(ix)"   ... materials's `that under certain circumstances an issuer may cease to publish annual reports and an investor may not continually have current financial information`
    ... materials's `explained in plain language and otherwise designed to communicate effectively and accurately`

@ref § 227.302(a)(1) — no investment commitment before the account is opened and e-delivery consented to
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary must not accept a commitment before the account is opened` intermediary MEANS
    IF       intermediary's `the investor has opened an account with the intermediary`
         AND intermediary's `the intermediary has obtained from the investor consent to electronic delivery of materials`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the intermediary`
         SHANT `accept an investment commitment`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.302(a)(1): an investment commitment was accepted before the investor opened an account and consented to electronic delivery"

@ref § 227.302(b)(1) — "In connection with establishing an account for an investor"
GIVEN materials IS AN `Educational materials`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's educational materials duty` materials MEANS
    PARTY `the intermediary`
    MUST  `deliver the educational materials to the investor`
          PROVIDED `the educational materials carry everything § 227.302(b)(1) requires` materials
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.302(b)(1): the educational materials were not delivered, or do not explain in plain language everything the paragraph requires"

@ref § 227.302(a)(2), (b)(2), (c), (d) — the remaining account-opening duties
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary complies with the rest of § 227.302` intermediary IF
        "(a)(2)" ... intermediary's `all subpart C information provided through electronic means`
    ... "(b)(2)" ... intermediary's `the most current version of the educational materials available on its platform at all times`
    ... "(b)(2)" ... (    NOT intermediary's `a material revision made to the educational materials`
                      OR  intermediary's `the revised educational materials made available to all investors before accepting any additional investment commitments`)
    ... "(c)"    ... intermediary's `the investor informed about the promoter disclosure requirement`
    ... "(d)"    ... intermediary's `the manner in which the intermediary is compensated clearly disclosed`


§§ `§ 227.304 Completion of offerings, cancellations and reconfirmations`

-- ENCODED BEFORE § 227.303 because § 227.303(e)(3)(i) CALLS it: funds may move
-- only "when ... the cancellation period as set forth in § 227.304 has
-- elapsed". Citation order would put § 227.303 first; the dependency runs the
-- other way.
--
-- AMBIGUITY paragraph (a) forbids CANCELLATION in the last 48 hours, and
-- paragraph (b)(2)(iii) contemplates the issuer choosing whether to ACCEPT
-- commitments in the corresponding window on an early close. Whether new
-- commitments may be accepted in the final 48 hours of an ORDINARY offering is
-- simply unstated. Reading (i): they may, since nothing forbids it, and the
-- (b)(2)(iii) notice exists because an early close shortens the window rather
-- than because acceptance is otherwise barred (taken here, by omission — no
-- limb of this encoding forbids it). Reading (ii): the 48-hour freeze is
-- symmetric. Not resolved by the text.
--
-- AMBIGUITY the part fixes THREE 21-day anchors — § 227.303(a)(2) (public
-- availability before any sale), § 227.303(e)(3)(i) (after publication, before
-- funds move) and § 227.304(b)(1) (the offering open) — and cross-refers
-- between them. Reading (i): all three run from the same event, the date the
-- information was first made publicly available, so they are one period seen
-- three times (taken here — § 227.304(b)(1) says "pursuant to § 227.303(a)",
-- which is that anchor). Reading (ii): three independent periods. The text
-- supplies one anchor date and three descriptions of it.

-- A GRANULARITY GAP, stated rather than hidden. § 227.304(a) draws its line at
-- FORTY-EIGHT HOURS before the deadline; every date in this module is a
-- calendar DATE, so the line below is drawn two whole days before the deadline
-- date instead. For a deadline with a time of day the two differ by up to
-- twenty-four hours, and the difference is on the investor's side of the line
-- (this encoding closes the window slightly early). Carrying the deadline as a
-- DATETIME would fix it; the regulation's own § 227.201(j)(1) and § 227.303(d)(4)
-- both contemplate a "date and time", so the fix is available and is a
-- modelling change, not a bug fix, and belongs in review.
@ref § 227.304(a) — "may cancel an investment commitment for any reason until 48 hours prior to the deadline"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the moment of cancellation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investor may still cancel for any reason` offering `the moment of cancellation` IF
    Day `the moment of cancellation`
        LESS THAN
    (Day (offering's `deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials`) MINUS (`the cancellation cut-off in hours` DIVIDED BY 24))

@ref § 227.304(b)(1) — "The offering remains open for a minimum of 21 days pursuant to § 227.303(a)"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`304(b)(1) — the offering remained open for at least 21 days` offering MEANS
        "(1)" ... (      Day (offering's `new offering deadline`)
                   MINUS Day (offering's `date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform`))
                  AT LEAST `the minimum public availability in days`

@ref § 227.304(b)(2)(i)-(iii) — the three things the early-close notice must say
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`304(b)(2) — the early-close notice says what it must` offering MEANS
        "(i)"   ... offering's `notice given of the new, anticipated deadline of the offering`
    ... "(ii)"  ... offering's `notice given of the right of investors to cancel investment commitments for any reason until 48 hours prior to the new offering deadline`
    ... "(iii)" ... offering's `notice given of whether the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline`

@ref § 227.304(b)(3) — "at least five business days after the notice ... is provided"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`304(b)(3) — the new deadline is at least five business days after the notice` offering MEANS
        "(3)" ... offering's `new offering deadline`
                  AT LEAST
                  `business days after` (offering's `date the notice of the new offering deadline was provided`) `five business days`

@ref § 227.304(b)(4) — "the issuer continues to meet or exceed the target offering amount"
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`304(b)(4) — the target is still met at the new deadline` offering MEANS
        "(4)" ... offering's `sum of the investment commitments` AT LEAST offering's `target offering amount`

@ref § 227.304(b) — the four conjunctive conditions on an early close
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issuer may close the offering early` offering IF
        offering's `sum of the investment commitments` AT LEAST offering's `target offering amount`
    AND offering's `new offering deadline` LESS THAN offering's `deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials`
    AND `304(b)(1) — the offering remained open for at least 21 days` offering
    AND `304(b)(2) — the early-close notice says what it must` offering
    AND `304(b)(3) — the new deadline is at least five business days after the notice` offering
    AND `304(b)(4) — the target is still met at the new deadline` offering

-- (c) is the richest deontic chain in the part: notice -> reconfirm within five
-- business days -> else cancel, notify and refund within a further five.
@ref § 227.304(c)(1) — material change, reconfirmation, and the consequences of failing to reconfirm
GIVEN offering   IS AN OfferingProfile
      commitment IS A CommitmentProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the material change reconfirmation chain` offering commitment MEANS
    IF   offering's `a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer`
    THEN PARTY  `the intermediary`
         MUST   `give or send the investor notice of the material change`
         WITHIN `five business days`
         HENCE  ( PARTY  `the investor`
                  MUST   `reconfirm the investment commitment`
                         PROVIDED commitment's `reconfirmed within five business days of receipt of the notice`
                  WITHIN `five business days`
                  HENCE  FULFILLED
                  LEST   ( PARTY  `the intermediary`
                           MUST   `give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount`
                           WITHIN `five business days`
                           HENCE  ( PARTY  `the intermediary`
                                    MUST   `direct the refund of investor funds`
                                    WITHIN `five business days`
                                    HENCE  FULFILLED
                                    LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(c)(1)(ii): the refund of investor funds was not directed within five business days of the failure to reconfirm" )
                           LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(c)(1)(i): the investor was not notified of the cancellation, its reason and the refund amount within five business days of the failure to reconfirm" ) )
         LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(c)(1): the investor was not given notice of the material change"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref § 227.304(c)(2) — the extension where a material change lands inside the last five business days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the extension required by § 227.304(c)(2)` MEANS
        "If material changes to the offering or to the information provided by the issuer regarding the offering occur within five business days of the maximum number of days that an offering is to remain open, the offering must be extended to allow for a period of five business days for the investor to reconfirm his or her investment."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.304(d)(1)-(3) — three parallel duties when the offering is not completed
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's duties when the offering is not completed` offering MEANS
    IF   offering's `the offering completed`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE ( PARTY  `the intermediary`
           MUST   `give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount`
           WITHIN `five business days`
           HENCE  FULFILLED
           LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(d)(1): each investor was not notified of the cancellation, its reason and the refund amount within five business days" )
         RAND
         ( PARTY  `the intermediary`
           MUST   `direct the refund of investor funds`
           WITHIN `five business days`
           HENCE  FULFILLED
           LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(d)(2): the refund of investor funds was not directed within five business days" )
         RAND
         ( PARTY  `the intermediary`
           MUST   `prevent investors from making investment commitments with respect to that offering`
           WITHIN `five business days`
           HENCE  FULFILLED
           LEST   BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.304(d)(3): investors were not prevented from making further investment commitments within five business days" )


§§ `§ 227.303 Requirements with respect to transactions`

@ref § 227.303(d)(1)-(4) — what the notice of an investment commitment must disclose
DECLARE `Commitment notice` HAS
    `the dollar amount of the investment commitment`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the price of the securities, if known`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name of the issuer`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date and time by which the investor may cancel the investment commitment`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref § 227.303(f)(1)(i)-(vi) — what the confirmation of a transaction must disclose
DECLARE `Transaction confirmation` HAS
    `the date of the transaction`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the type of security that the investor is purchasing`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the identity, price, and number of securities purchased by the investor, the number sold by the issuer and the prices at which they were sold`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `if a debt security, the interest rate and the yield to maturity calculated from the price paid and the maturity date`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `if a callable security, the first date that the security can be called by the issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the source, form and amount of any remuneration received or to be received by the intermediary in connection with the transaction`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref § 227.303(e)(2)(i)-(ii) — the two kinds of qualified third party
DECLARE `qualified third party` IS ONE OF
    `a registered broker or dealer that carries customer or broker or dealer accounts and holds funds or securities for those persons`
    `a bank or credit union insured by the National Credit Union Administration that has agreed in writing to hold the funds in escrow or to maintain an account for the exclusive benefit of investors and the issuer`

@ref § 227.303(a)(1)-(4) — issuer information, made publicly available
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
      offering     IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the date of the first sale` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary has made the issuer information publicly available as § 227.303(a) requires` intermediary offering `the date of the first sale` IF
        "(1)" ... intermediary's `the issuer information made publicly available on its platform in a manner that reasonably permits a person to save, download, or otherwise store it`
    ... "(2)" ... (      Day `the date of the first sale`
                   MINUS Day (offering's `date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform`))
                  AT LEAST `the minimum public availability in days`
    ... "(3)" ... intermediary's `the issuer information remains publicly available until the offer and sale is completed or cancelled`
    ... "(4)" ... intermediary's `no person required to establish an account with the intermediary to access that information`

@ref § 227.303(b)(2)(ii)(A)-(C) — the questionnaire
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the questionnaire demonstrates what § 227.303(b)(2)(ii) requires` intermediary MEANS
        "(A)" ... intermediary's `a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding of the restrictions on cancellation`
    ... "(B)" ... intermediary's `a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that it may be difficult to resell the securities`
    ... "(C)" ... intermediary's `a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that investing involves risk and that he or she should not invest funds he or she cannot afford to lose`

@ref § 227.303(b)(1)-(2) — "Each time before accepting any investment commitment"
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary has qualified the investor as § 227.303(b) requires` intermediary IF
        "(1)"     ... intermediary's `a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations`
    ... "(2)(i)"  ... intermediary's `a representation obtained that the investor has reviewed the educational materials, understands that the entire investment may be lost, and is in a financial condition to bear the loss`
    ... "(2)(ii)" ... `the questionnaire demonstrates what § 227.303(b)(2)(ii) requires` intermediary

@ref § 227.303(c)(1)-(4) — communication channels
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary's communication channels comply with § 227.303(c)` intermediary IF
        intermediary's `communication channels provided on its platform`
    ... "(1)" ... (    NOT `the intermediary is a funding portal` intermediary
                   OR  intermediary's `it does not participate in those communications other than to establish guidelines and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications`)
    ... "(2)" ... intermediary's `public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels`
    ... "(3)" ... intermediary's `posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account`
    ... "(4)" ... intermediary's `each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer`

@ref § 227.303(d)(1)-(4) — "must promptly, upon receipt of an investment commitment"
GIVEN notice IS A `Commitment notice`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's notice-of-commitment duty` notice MEANS
    PARTY `the intermediary`
    MUST  `give or send the investor notice of the investment commitment`
          PROVIDED     "(1)" ... notice's `the dollar amount of the investment commitment`
                   AND "(2)" ... notice's `the price of the securities, if known`
                   AND "(3)" ... notice's `the name of the issuer`
                   AND "(4)" ... notice's `the date and time by which the investor may cancel the investment commitment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.303(d): the investor was not promptly given a notification disclosing the amount, the price, the issuer and the cancellation deadline"

@ref § 227.303(e)(1)-(2) — where the money goes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the maintenance and transmission of funds under § 227.303(e)(1)-(2)` MEANS
        "(1) An intermediary that is a registered broker must comply with the requirements of 17 CFR 240.15c2-4."
    ... "(2) An intermediary that is a funding portal must direct investors to transmit the money or other consideration directly to a qualified third party that has agreed in writing to hold the funds for the benefit of, and to promptly transmit or return the funds to, the persons entitled thereto in accordance with paragraph (e)(3) of this section."
    ... TRUE

-- (e)(3)(i) is the FUND-FLOW GATE, and it is the place § 227.303 calls
-- § 227.304: funds move only when the target is met, the cancellation period
-- of § 227.304 has elapsed, and — a floor the proviso adds on top of both —
-- never earlier than 21 days after publication.
@ref § 227.303(e)(3)(i) — the three conjunctive conditions on transmitting funds to the issuer
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the date of the proposed transmission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the funding portal may direct the transmission of funds to the issuer` offering `the date of the proposed transmission` IF
        offering's `sum of the investment commitments` AT LEAST offering's `target offering amount`
    AND NOT `the investor may still cancel for any reason` offering `the date of the proposed transmission`
    AND (      Day `the date of the proposed transmission`
         MINUS Day (offering's `date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform`))
        AT LEAST `the minimum public availability in days`

@ref § 227.303(e)(3)(i)-(iii) — the funding portal's direction to the qualified third party
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile
      `the date of the proposed transmission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the funding portal's fund-flow duty` offering `the date of the proposed transmission` MEANS
    IF   `the funding portal may direct the transmission of funds to the issuer` offering `the date of the proposed transmission`
    THEN PARTY `the funding portal`
         MAY   `direct the qualified third party to transmit the funds to the issuer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the funding portal`
         MUST  `direct the refund of investor funds`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.303(e)(3)(ii)-(iii): funds were neither transmitted lawfully nor returned to investors on cancellation or on failure to complete the offering"

@ref § 227.303(f)(1)(i)-(vi) — what the confirmation must disclose
GIVEN confirmation IS A `Transaction confirmation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires` confirmation MEANS
        "(i)"   ... confirmation's `the date of the transaction`
    ... "(ii)"  ... confirmation's `the type of security that the investor is purchasing`
    ... "(iii)" ... confirmation's `the identity, price, and number of securities purchased by the investor, the number sold by the issuer and the prices at which they were sold`
    ... "(iv)"  ... confirmation's `if a debt security, the interest rate and the yield to maturity calculated from the price paid and the maturity date`
    ... "(v)"   ... confirmation's `if a callable security, the first date that the security can be called by the issuer`
    ... "(vi)"  ... confirmation's `the source, form and amount of any remuneration received or to be received by the intermediary in connection with the transaction`

@ref § 227.303(f)(1) — "at or before the completion of a transaction"
GIVEN confirmation IS A `Transaction confirmation`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's transaction confirmation duty` confirmation MEANS
    PARTY `the intermediary`
    MUST  `give or send the investor confirmation of the transaction`
          PROVIDED `the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires` confirmation
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.303(f)(1): the investor was not given a notification disclosing all six required items at or before the completion of the transaction"

@ref § 227.303(f)(2) — compliance with (f)(1) exempts from § 240.10b-10
GIVEN confirmation IS A `Transaction confirmation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary is exempt from § 240.10b-10 for this transaction` confirmation IF
    `the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires` confirmation


§§ `§ 227.301 Measures to reduce risk of fraud`

-- ENCODED AFTER §§ 227.503 and 227.303 because it calls both: (c)(1) turns on
-- a § 227.503 disqualification and (c)(2) requires the return of funds, which
-- is § 227.303(e)'s machinery.
--
-- AMBIGUITY (c)(2) turns on whether the issuer or the offering "presents the
-- potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor
-- protection", and § 227.303(d) and § 227.301(c)(2) both require action
-- "promptly". Both are vague with no competing parse: one reading, an
-- undecidable boundary. They arrive as facts.

@ref § 227.301(a)-(b) — the two reasonable-basis duties, and the transfer-agent deeming
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the intermediary has the reasonable bases § 227.301(a)-(b) requires` intermediary IF
        "(a)" ... intermediary's `a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`
    ... "(b)" ... (    intermediary's `a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer has established means to keep accurate records of the holders of the securities`
                   OR  intermediary's `the issuer has engaged the services of a transfer agent registered under section 17A of the Exchange Act`)

@ref § 227.301(c)(1) — deny access on a reasonable belief of a § 227.503 disqualification
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's duty to deny access for a disqualification` intermediary MEANS
    IF   "(1)" ... intermediary's `a reasonable basis for believing that a covered person is subject to a disqualification under § 227.503`
    THEN PARTY `the intermediary`
         MUST  `deny access to its platform to the issuer`
               PROVIDED intermediary's `a background and securities enforcement regulatory history check conducted on the issuer and on each officer, director and twenty percent beneficial owner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.301(c)(1): access was not denied to an issuer reasonably believed to be subject to a § 227.503 disqualification, or the minimum background and regulatory-history check was not conducted"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref § 227.301(c)(2) — deny access, and on post-grant awareness remove, cancel and return
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary's duty on a fraud or investor-protection concern` intermediary MEANS
    IF        "(2)" ... intermediary's `a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection`
          OR  intermediary's `unable to adequately or effectively assess the risk of fraud of the issuer or its potential offering`
    THEN IF   intermediary's `became aware of that information after granting access`
         THEN PARTY `the intermediary`
              MUST  `remove the offering from its platform, cancel the offering, and return the funds committed by investors`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.301(c)(2): on becoming aware after granting access, the offering was not promptly removed and cancelled and the committed funds were not returned"
         ELSE PARTY `the intermediary`
              MUST  `deny access to its platform to the issuer`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.301(c)(2): access was not denied although the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or raises concerns about investor protection"
    ELSE FULFILLED


§§ `§ 227.305 Payments to third parties`

@ref § 227.305(a) — the prohibition on paying for investor personally identifiable information
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the intermediary must not pay for investor personal information` MEANS
    PARTY `the intermediary`
    SHANT `compensate a person for the personally identifiable information of an investor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the intermediary` BECAUSE "§ 227.305(a): a person was compensated for providing the personally identifiable information of an investor or potential investor"

-- (b) is a pure definition carrier. Nothing in this module tests it, because
-- nothing in the part turns on the boundary — the prohibition is absolute.
@ref § 227.305(b) — "personally identifiable information"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "personally identifiable information"` MEANS
        "For purposes of this rule, personally identifiable information means information that can be used to distinguish or trace an individual's identity, either alone or when combined with other personal or identifying information that is linked or linkable to a specific individual."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.400 Registration of funding portals`

@ref § 227.400(a)(1)-(2) — "The registration will be effective the later of"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the date the funding portal's registration becomes effective` portal IS
    IF   Day `thirty calendar days after receipt` AT LEAST Day (portal's `date approved for membership by a registered national securities association`)
    THEN `thirty calendar days after receipt`
    ELSE portal's `date approved for membership by a registered national securities association`
    WHERE
        `thirty calendar days after receipt` MEANS
            Date (Day (portal's `date the registration was received by the Commission`) PLUS `the portal registration effectiveness in days`)

@ref § 227.400(a) — the two things registration requires
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the funding portal's registration duty` portal MEANS
    PARTY `the funding portal`
    MUST  `register on Form Funding Portal and become a member of a national securities association`
          PROVIDED portal's `a complete Form Funding Portal filed with the Commission`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.400(a): a complete Form Funding Portal was not filed with the Commission, or the portal did not become a member of a registered national securities association"

@ref § 227.400(b) — "within 30 days of any of the information ... becoming inaccurate"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the funding portal's amendment duty` portal MEANS
    IF   portal's `information previously submitted on Form Funding Portal has become inaccurate`
    THEN PARTY  `the funding portal`
         MUST   `file an amendment to Form Funding Portal`
         WITHIN `the portal amendment window in days`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.400(b): no amendment to Form Funding Portal was filed within 30 days of the information becoming inaccurate"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref § 227.400(c)(1) proviso — "deemed withdrawn 45 days after registration ... is filed by the successor"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the date the predecessor's registration is deemed withdrawn` portal IS
    Date (Day (portal's `date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal`) PLUS `the predecessor deemed withdrawal in days`)

@ref § 227.400(c)(1)-(2) — succession
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the predecessor's registration remains effective as the successor's` portal IF
        portal's `succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal`
    AND (      Day (portal's `date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal`)
         MINUS Day (portal's `date of the succession`))
        AT MOST `the portal amendment window in days`

@ref § 227.400(c)(2) — the pure-form succession may be handled by amendment instead
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pure-form succession alternative in § 227.400(c)(2)` MEANS
        "if a funding portal succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal and the succession is based solely on a change of the predecessor's date or state of incorporation, form of organization, or composition of a partnership, the successor may, within 30 days after the succession, amend the registration of the predecessor on Form Funding Portal to reflect these changes."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.400(d) — "effective on the later of 30 days after receipt ... or such longer period"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the date the withdrawal becomes effective` portal IS
    IF   Day `thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal` AT LEAST Day (portal's `a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order`)
    THEN `thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal`
    ELSE portal's `a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order`
    WHERE
        `thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal` MEANS
            Date (Day (portal's `date the withdrawal was received by the Commission`) PLUS `the portal registration effectiveness in days`)

@ref § 227.400(d) — "must promptly file a withdrawal ... upon ceasing to operate as a funding portal"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the funding portal's withdrawal duty` portal MEANS
    IF   portal's `has ceased to operate as a funding portal`
    THEN PARTY `the funding portal`
         MUST  `file a withdrawal of registration on Form Funding Portal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.400(d): a withdrawal of registration was not promptly filed on ceasing to operate as a funding portal"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref § 227.400(e) — when an application or report is filed, and the duplicate originals
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`when a Form Funding Portal is filed, and the duplicate originals` MEANS
        "The applications and reports provided for in this section shall be considered filed when a complete Form Funding Portal is submitted with the Commission."
    ... "Duplicate originals of the applications and reports provided for in this section must be filed with surveillance personnel designated by any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.400(f) and (f)(1) — nonresident funding portals
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the nonresident information-sharing condition is met` portal MEANS
        NOT portal's `nonresident`
    ..  portal's `an information sharing arrangement in place between the Commission and the competent regulator`

@ref § 227.400(f)(1) — "nonresident funding portal"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of "nonresident funding portal"` MEANS
        "For purposes of this section, the term nonresident funding portal shall mean a funding portal incorporated in or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction outside of the United States or its territories, or having its principal place of business in any place not in the United States or its territories."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.400(f)(2)(i)-(v) — the power of attorney and the agent for service of process
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nonresident portal's power-of-attorney obligations are met` portal IF
        "(i)"   ... portal's `a written consent and power of attorney appointing an agent in the United States obtained`
    ... "(ii)"  ... portal's `the name and address of its United States agent for service of process furnished on Schedule C`
    ... "(iii)" ... portal's `a change of agent communicated promptly to the Commission through amendment of Schedule C`
    ... "(iv)"  ... portal's `a successor agent for service of process promptly appointed where required`
    ... "(v)"   ... portal's `the written consent and power of attorney maintained as part of its books and records for at least three years after termination`

@ref § 227.400(f)(3)(i)(A)-(B) — the certification and the opinion of counsel
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nonresident portal's books-and-records certification is in place` portal IF
        "(A)" ... portal's `certified on Schedule C that it can and will provide prompt access to its books and records and submit to onsite inspection and examination`
    ... "(B)" ... portal's `an opinion of counsel provided that it can, as a matter of law, provide that access and submit to that inspection`

@ref § 227.400(f)(3)(ii) — "within 90 days after any changes in the legal or regulatory framework"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the nonresident portal's re-certification duty` portal MEANS
    IF       portal's `nonresident`
         AND portal's `a change in the legal or regulatory framework affecting that access or inspection`
    THEN PARTY  `the funding portal`
         MUST   `re-certify on Schedule C to Form Funding Portal`
         WITHIN `the re-certification window in days`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.400(f)(3)(ii): the portal did not re-certify on Schedule C, with a revised opinion of counsel, within 90 days of the change in the legal or regulatory framework"
    ELSE FULFILLED


§§ `§ 227.401 Exemption`

@ref § 227.401
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the funding portal is exempt from broker registration under section 15(a)(1)` portal IF
        "A funding portal that is registered with the Commission pursuant to § 227.400 is exempt from the broker registration requirements of section 15(a)(1) of the Exchange Act in connection with its activities as a funding portal."
    ... portal's `a complete Form Funding Portal filed with the Commission`


§§ `§ 227.403 Compliance`

@ref § 227.403(a)-(c)
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the funding portal complies with § 227.403` portal IF
        "(a)" ... portal's `written policies and procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with the federal securities laws implemented`
    ... "(b)" ... portal's `complies with the requirements of part 248 of this chapter as they apply to brokers`
    ... "(c)" ... portal's `permits the examination and inspection of its business and business operations`


§§ `§ 227.404 Records to be made and kept by funding portals`

-- Paragraph (f) is a REAL computation and not a pointer: "Where 31 CFR chapter
-- X and § 227.404(a) and (b) require the same records or reports to be
-- preserved for different periods of time, such records or reports shall be
-- preserved for the longer period of time." That is a maximum over two
-- retention periods, and it is encoded as one.
@ref § 227.404(a) with (f) — "such records or reports shall be preserved for the longer period of time"
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the governing retention period in years` portal IS
    IF   portal's `subject to the requirements of the Currency and Foreign Transactions Reporting Act of 1970`
    THEN max `the record retention in years` (portal's `the retention period required by 31 CFR chapter X in years`)
    ELSE `the record retention in years`

@ref § 227.404(a)(1)-(9) — the nine record categories
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the nine categories of records § 227.404(a) requires` MEANS
        "(1) All records related to an investor who purchases or attempts to purchase securities through the funding portal;"
    ... "(2) All records related to issuers who offer and sell or attempt to offer and sell securities through the funding portal and the control persons of such issuers;"
    ... "(3) Records of all communications that occur on or through its platform;"
    ... "(4) All records related to persons that use communication channels provided by a funding portal to promote an issuer's securities or communicate with potential investors;"
    ... "(5) All records required to demonstrate compliance with the requirements of subparts C and D of this part;"
    ... "(6) All notices provided by such funding portal to issuers and investors generally through the funding portal's platform or otherwise;"
    ... "(7) All written agreements (or copies thereof) entered into by such funding portal relating to its business as such;"
    ... "(8) All daily, monthly and quarterly summaries of transactions effected through the funding portal;"
    ... "(9) A log reflecting the progress of each issuer who offers or sells securities through the funding portal toward meeting the target offering amount."
    ... TRUE

-- NOTE the seam between the computation above and the guard below. The (a)
-- field asserts preservation "for five years, the first two years in an easily
-- accessible place" — paragraph (a)'s OWN period — while the governing period
-- may be longer under paragraph (f). The duty is therefore satisfiable on
-- paragraph (a)'s terms while paragraph (f) still requires more, and closing
-- that seam would mean carrying the actual retention achieved as a number
-- rather than a boolean. That is a modelling change and it is not made here.
@ref § 227.404(a)-(e)
GIVEN portal IS A FundingPortalProfile
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Reg CF party` `Reg CF act`
`the funding portal's recordkeeping duty` portal MEANS
    ( PARTY `the funding portal`
      MUST  `make and preserve the records required by § 227.404`
            PROVIDED     "(a)" ... portal's `the nine categories of records made and preserved for five years, the first two years in an easily accessible place`
                     AND "(b)" ... portal's `organizational documents made and preserved during the operation of the funding portal and of any successor`
                     AND "(c)" ... portal's `records produced, reproduced and maintained in the original, non-alterable format or as permitted under § 240.17a-4(f)`
                     AND "(d)" ... portal's `a written undertaking filed with the registered national securities association where a third party maintains the records`
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST  BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.404(a)-(d): the required records were not made, preserved for the governing period, kept in a non-alterable format, or covered by the required third-party undertaking" )
    RAND
    ( PARTY `the funding portal`
      MUST  `permit the examination and inspection of its business and business operations`
            PROVIDED "(e)" ... portal's `records furnished promptly to the Commission and the association on request`
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST  BREACH BY `the funding portal` BECAUSE "§ 227.404(e): records were not furnished promptly to the Commission or to the registered national securities association on request" )

@ref § 227.404(d) — the prescribed form of words for a third-party undertaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the third-party undertaking § 227.404(d) prescribes` MEANS
        "With respect to any books and records maintained or preserved on behalf of [name of funding portal], the undersigned hereby acknowledges that the books and records are the property of [name of funding portal], and hereby undertakes to permit examination of such books and records at any time, or from time to time, during business hours by representatives of the Securities and Exchange Commission and the registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member, and to promptly furnish to the Commission, its representatives, and the registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member, a true, correct, complete and current hard copy of any, all, or any part of, such books and records."
    ... TRUE


§§ `§ 227.402 Conditional safe harbor`

-- ENCODED LAST in subpart D because paragraphs (b)(10) and (b)(13) point at
-- § 227.301(c)(2) and § 227.303(e). Note precisely what those pointers are
-- here: NOT calls on those rules' outcomes but conditions carried on the
-- activity record — (b)(10) permits the denial or cancellation only where the
-- portal has the § 227.301(c)(2) reasonable belief, and (b)(13) permits the
-- direction only of the qualified third party § 227.303(e) requires. Under the
-- outcome-versus-compliance rule this module follows, they are facts about the
-- activity, so § 227.402 does not in fact depend on those sections; the
-- ordering is citation-adjacency rather than a forced dependency.
--
-- (a) is FRAMING, not a test: it restates the section 3(a)(80) prohibitions,
-- says no presumption of violation arises from an activity outside the list,
-- and preserves the antifraud provisions. Encoded as a definition carrier,
-- because turning "no presumption shall arise" into a boolean would assert
-- something the paragraph is careful not to assert.

@ref § 227.402(a)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the framing of the conditional safe harbor in § 227.402(a)` MEANS
        "Under section 3(a)(80) of the Exchange Act, a funding portal acting as an intermediary in a transaction involving the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act may not: offer investment advice or recommendations; solicit purchases, sales, or offers to buy the securities offered or displayed on its platform or portal; compensate employees, agents, or other persons for such solicitation or based on the sale of securities displayed or referenced on its platform or portal; hold, manage, possess, or otherwise handle investor funds or securities; or engage in such other activities as the Commission, by rule, determines appropriate."
    ... "No presumption shall arise that a funding portal has violated the prohibitions under section 3(a)(80) of the Exchange Act or this part by reason of the funding portal or its associated persons engaging in activities in connection with the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act that do not meet the conditions specified in paragraph (b) of this section."
    ... "The antifraud provisions and all other applicable provisions of the federal securities laws continue to apply to the activities described in paragraph (b) of this section."
    ... TRUE

@ref § 227.402(b)(1)-(13) — the thirteen permitted activities
DECLARE `funding portal activity` IS ONE OF
    `determining whether and under what terms to allow an issuer to offer and sell securities through its platform`
    `applying objective criteria to highlight offerings on the platform`
    `providing search, sort or categorisation tools`
    `providing communication channels`
    `advising an issuer about the structure or content of the issuer's offering`
    `compensating a third party for referring a person to the funding portal`
    `paying compensation to a registered broker or dealer for services`
    `receiving compensation from a registered broker or dealer for services`
    `advertising the existence of the funding portal and identifying issuers or offerings on the basis of objective criteria`
    `denying access to the platform to, or cancelling an offering of, an issuer pursuant to § 227.301(c)(2)`
    `accepting, on behalf of an issuer, an investment commitment`
    `directing investors where to transmit funds or remit payment`
    `directing a qualified third party to release proceeds to an issuer or to return proceeds to investors`

@ref § 227.402(b)(1)-(13) — the conditions attached to those activities
DECLARE `Portal activity` HAS
    `the activity`                                                                   IS A `funding portal activity`
    `the funding portal otherwise complies with this part`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the criteria are reasonably designed to highlight or identify a broad selection of issuers, are applied consistently to all issuers and offerings, and are clearly displayed on the platform`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the funding portal does not receive special or additional compensation for highlighting or identifying one or more issuers or offerings`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it does not participate in the communications other than to establish guidelines for communication and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account on its platform`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the third party does not provide the funding portal with personally identifiable information of any potential investor`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the referral compensation, other than that paid to a registered broker or dealer, is not based on the purchase or sale of a security offered on or through the platform`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the services are provided pursuant to a written agreement between the funding portal and the registered broker or dealer`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the services and compensation are permitted under this part`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the services and compensation comply with the rules of any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref § 227.402(b)(2) and (b)(9) — the highlighting and advertising conditions
GIVEN activity IS A `Portal activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the objective-criteria conditions are met` activity MEANS
        activity's `the criteria are reasonably designed to highlight or identify a broad selection of issuers, are applied consistently to all issuers and offerings, and are clearly displayed on the platform`
    ... activity's `the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment`
    ... activity's `the funding portal does not receive special or additional compensation for highlighting or identifying one or more issuers or offerings`

@ref § 227.402(b)(4) — the communication-channel conditions
GIVEN activity IS A `Portal activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the communication-channel conditions are met` activity MEANS
        "(i)"   ... activity's `it does not participate in the communications other than to establish guidelines for communication and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications`
    ... "(ii)"  ... activity's `public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels`
    ... "(iii)" ... activity's `posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account on its platform`
    ... "(iv)"  ... activity's `each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer`

@ref § 227.402(b)(7)-(8) — the broker-dealer compensation conditions
GIVEN activity IS A `Portal activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met` activity MEANS
        "(i)"   ... activity's `the services are provided pursuant to a written agreement between the funding portal and the registered broker or dealer`
    ... "(ii)"  ... activity's `the services and compensation are permitted under this part`
    ... "(iii)" ... activity's `the services and compensation comply with the rules of any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member`

@ref § 227.402(b)(1)-(13)
GIVEN activity IS A `Portal activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity falls within the funding portal safe harbour` activity IS
    CONSIDER activity's `the activity`
    WHEN `determining whether and under what terms to allow an issuer to offer and sell securities through its platform`
         THEN activity's `the funding portal otherwise complies with this part`
    WHEN `applying objective criteria to highlight offerings on the platform`
         THEN `the objective-criteria conditions are met` activity
    WHEN `providing search, sort or categorisation tools`
         THEN activity's `the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment`
    WHEN `providing communication channels`
         THEN `the communication-channel conditions are met` activity
    WHEN `advising an issuer about the structure or content of the issuer's offering`
         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `compensating a third party for referring a person to the funding portal`
         THEN     activity's `the third party does not provide the funding portal with personally identifiable information of any potential investor`
              AND activity's `the referral compensation, other than that paid to a registered broker or dealer, is not based on the purchase or sale of a security offered on or through the platform`
    WHEN `paying compensation to a registered broker or dealer for services`
         THEN `the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met` activity
    WHEN `receiving compensation from a registered broker or dealer for services`
         THEN `the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met` activity
    WHEN `advertising the existence of the funding portal and identifying issuers or offerings on the basis of objective criteria`
         THEN `the objective-criteria conditions are met` activity
    WHEN `denying access to the platform to, or cancelling an offering of, an issuer pursuant to § 227.301(c)(2)`
         THEN activity's `a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection`
    WHEN `accepting, on behalf of an issuer, an investment commitment`
         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `directing investors where to transmit funds or remit payment`
         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `directing a qualified third party to release proceeds to an issuer or to return proceeds to investors`
         THEN TRUE


§§ `§ 227.502 Insignificant deviations from a term, condition or requirement of this part`

-- ENCODED LAST, because it quantifies over "a term, condition, or requirement
-- of this part" — everything above.
--
-- AMBIGUITY paragraph (a)(3) is one sentence with two limbs and no comma to
-- separate them cleanly: "The issuer did not know of such failure where the
-- failure to comply ... was the result of the failure of the intermediary to
-- comply with the requirements of section 4A(a) ..., or such failure by the
-- intermediary occurred solely in offerings other than the issuer's offering."
-- Reading (i): the paragraph bites only when the failure was the
-- intermediary's, and is then satisfied either by the issuer's ignorance or by
-- the intermediary's failure having been confined to other offerings (taken
-- here). Reading (ii): "the issuer did not know of such failure" is a
-- freestanding requirement in every case, and the "where ..." clause merely
-- describes the commonest situation. The two differ on every failure that was
-- the issuer's own and that the issuer knew about.
--
-- AMBIGUITY "insignificant with respect to the offering as a whole" is vague
-- with no competing parse. It arrives as a fact.

@ref § 227.502(a)(3)
GIVEN claim IS A DeviationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`502(a)(3) — the issuer's knowledge limb` claim MEANS
        "(3)" ... NOT claim's `the failure resulted from the intermediary's failure to comply with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related rules`
    ..  claim's `the issuer did not know of such failure`
    ..  claim's `the intermediary's failure occurred solely in offerings other than the issuer's offering`

@ref § 227.502(a)(1)-(3)
GIVEN claim IS A DeviationClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the failure to comply does not cost the exemption for a particular purchaser` claim IF
        "(1)" ... claim's `the failure to comply was insignificant with respect to the offering as a whole`
    ... "(2)" ... claim's `the issuer made a good faith and reasonable attempt to comply with all applicable terms, conditions and requirements of this part`
    ... `502(a)(3) — the issuer's knowledge limb` claim

-- (b) is not operative on any question this module answers — it preserves the
-- Commission's enforcement powers rather than deciding anything — so it is
-- carried inert rather than made into a predicate that no fact could falsify.
@ref § 227.502(b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`§ 227.502(b) preserves the Commission's enforcement powers` MEANS
        "Paragraph (a) of this section shall not preclude the Commission from bringing an enforcement action seeking any appropriate relief for an issuer's failure to comply with all applicable terms, conditions and requirements of this part."
    ... TRUE


§§ `Entry points — the decisions a caller actually asks for`

-- These are thin wrappers, not new rules: each one names a question a reader of
-- Regulation Crowdfunding actually has, gives every parameter an @desc a
-- caller can act on, and delegates to the encoded provision above. The
-- decisions themselves stay where the regulation puts them.
--
-- ONE CONSEQUENCE OF THE ENCODING FLOOR, stated here because it shows up at
-- the API boundary and nowhere else: every decision that reads one of the
-- seven inflation-indexed constants transitively references the module-level
-- ASSUME `no encoding of Part 227 exists for rule dates before 2022-09-20`,
-- and a referenced ASSUME is promoted to a parameter of an exported function.
-- So a caller of the money decisions is asked for that binding. It is never
-- consumed for a rule date on or after 2022-09-20 — the BRANCH selects the
-- other arm — but it is asked for, and that is the price of a curated refusal
-- rather than a silently wrong number below the floor.

@export Decide whether the Regulation Crowdfunding exemption under Securities Act section 4(a)(6) is available for a particular sale of securities by a particular issuer to a particular investor.
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation   @desc Which reading of the six contested provisions to apply. Use `the staff reading` for the SEC staff's published interpretations, `the text alone` for the regulation's own words.
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile    @desc The issuer's eligibility facts, its prior sales under section 4(a)(6), and its covered persons.
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile  @desc The offering: target amount, deadline, intermediary arrangements and disclosure.
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile  @desc The purchaser's accredited-investor status, income, net worth and prior crowdfunding investments.
      `this investment` IS A NUMBER   @desc The dollar amount this investor is committing in this transaction.
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE  @desc The date of the offer or sale being tested, ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-16.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exemption is available` interp issuer offering investor `this investment` `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
    `the crowdfunding exemption is available` interp issuer offering investor `this investment` `the date of the offer or sale`

@export Calculate the maximum dollar amount a particular investor may invest across all Regulation Crowdfunding issuers in a 12-month period, under 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2).
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation  @desc Which reading to apply; see `the staff reading` and `the text alone`.
      investor IS AN InvestorProfile @desc The investor's annual income, net worth, and — for an entity — revenue and net assets.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the investment limit` interp investor MEANS
    `the investment limit for the investor` interp investor

@export Calculate how much more an issuer may raise under Regulation Crowdfunding before hitting the $5,000,000 rolling 12-month cap in 17 CFR 227.100(a)(1).
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation  @desc Which reading to apply; the answer differs between `the staff reading` (rolling from each closing) and `the text alone`.
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile   @desc The issuer, including its list of prior closings under section 4(a)(6).
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile @desc The contemplated offering.
      `the date of the offer or sale` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the headroom is measured, ISO 8601.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the issuer's remaining capacity under the twelve month cap` interp issuer offering `the date of the offer or sale` MEANS
    `the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap` interp issuer offering `the date of the offer or sale`

@export Determine which level of financial statements an issuer must provide with its Regulation Crowdfunding offering statement — tax return information, reviewed, or audited — under 17 CFR 227.201(t).
GIVEN interp   IS AN Interpretation  @desc Which reading to apply; affects how the 12-month aggregation is measured.
      issuer   IS AN IssuerProfile   @desc The issuer, including whether it has previously sold securities under section 4(a)(6).
      offering IS AN OfferingProfile @desc The offering, including the target amount and any maximum the issuer will accept.
GIVETH A `financial statement requirement`
`the financial statement level required` interp issuer offering MEANS
    `the financial statements required` interp issuer offering

@export Determine whether an issuer must keep filing Regulation Crowdfunding annual reports, or may stop, under 17 CFR 227.202(b).
GIVEN interp IS AN Interpretation @desc Which reading to apply. This decision is where the crowdfunding-vehicle look-through fork bites: `the staff reading` counts the investors behind a vehicle, `the text alone` counts the register.
      issuer IS AN IssuerProfile  @desc The issuer, including its holder counts, total assets and annual reports filed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ongoing reporting obligation continues` interp issuer MEANS
    NOT `the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting` interp issuer

@export Determine whether securities acquired in a Regulation Crowdfunding offering may lawfully be transferred, under the one-year resale restriction in 17 CFR 227.501.
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer @desc The proposed transfer: the issuance date, the transfer date, and which of the four statutory exceptions (if any) it falls within.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the resale is permitted` transfer MEANS
    `the transfer is permitted` transfer

@export Determine whether a covered person's criminal, regulatory or administrative history disqualifies an issuer's Regulation Crowdfunding offering under 17 CFR 227.503(a).
GIVEN person IS A CoveredPerson @desc The covered person, their class, and the events and dates alleged against them.
      `the filing` IS A DATE    @desc The date the offering statement (Form C) was filed, ISO 8601. Every lookback in 17 CFR 227.503(a) is measured back from this date.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a disqualifying covered person` person `the filing` MEANS
    `the covered person is disqualified` person `the filing`

@export Determine whether an issuer that has reached its target offering amount may close its Regulation Crowdfunding offering before the deadline in its offering materials, under 17 CFR 227.304(b).
GIVEN offering IS AN OfferingProfile @desc The offering, including the proposed new deadline, the notice given, and the commitments received.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offering may be closed early` offering MEANS
    `the issuer may close the offering early` offering

@export Determine whether a person is qualified to act as an intermediary in a Regulation Crowdfunding transaction, under 17 CFR 227.300(a).
GIVEN intermediary IS AN IntermediaryProfile @desc The candidate intermediary's registration and association membership.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may act as an intermediary` intermediary MEANS
    `the person qualifies to act as an intermediary` intermediary

@export Determine whether an activity a funding portal proposes to undertake falls within the conditional safe harbor in 17 CFR 227.402(b), so that it does not breach the Exchange Act section 3(a)(80) prohibitions.
GIVEN activity IS A `Portal activity` @desc The activity and the conditions attached to it by 17 CFR 227.402(b).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the funding portal activity is within the safe harbour` activity MEANS
    `the activity falls within the funding portal safe harbour` activity


§§ `Fixtures — constructors that vary one thing at a time`

-- L4 builds records only from a TYPE NAME (`InvestorProfile WITH ...`); there
-- is no in-place record-update operator. So each fixture below is a
-- GIVEN-parameterised constructor that supplies every field and exposes the
-- ones a test needs to vary.

@ref test fixture — an investor, varying the quantities § 227.100(a)(2) measures
GIVEN `who`              IS A STRING
      `natural`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `income`           IS A NUMBER
      `worth`            IS A NUMBER
      `revenue`          IS A NUMBER
      `assets`           IS A NUMBER
      `already invested` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN InvestorProfile
`an investor` `who` `natural` `income` `worth` `revenue` `assets` `already invested` MEANS InvestorProfile WITH
    name                                                                            IS `who`
    `a natural person`                                                              IS `natural`
    `within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be`  IS FALSE
    `annual income for the calendar year`                                           IS `income`
    `annual income for the investor's own fiscal year`                              IS `income`
    `revenue for the most recent fiscal year`                                       IS `revenue`
    `net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end`                              IS `assets`
    `total assets other than the primary residence`                                 IS `worth`
    `total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence`    IS 0
    `estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale`  IS 0
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale`  IS 0
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale`  IS 0
    `the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence`  IS FALSE
    `the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities`   IS FALSE
    `that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010`                            IS FALSE
    `qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired`  IS FALSE
    `held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010`   IS FALSE
    `net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments`              IS `worth`
    `individual income in each of the two most recent years`                        IS `income`
    `joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years`       IS 0
    `a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year`  IS TRUE
    `aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months`  IS `already invested`
    `annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse`      IS FALSE
    `the aggregate investment of the investor spouses`                              IS 0

@ref test fixture — a covered person with a single conviction
GIVEN `who`                  IS A STRING
      `their class`          IS A `covered person class`
      `convicted`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `when convicted`       IS A DATE
GIVETH A CoveredPerson
`a covered person convicted of securities fraud` `who` `their class` `convicted` `when convicted` MEANS CoveredPerson WITH
    name  IS `who`
    class IS `their class`
    `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor in connection with the purchase or sale of any security`  IS `convicted`
    `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor involving the making of a false filing with the Commission`  IS FALSE
    `convicted of a felony or misdemeanor arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities`  IS FALSE
    `date of the conviction`  IS `when convicted`
    `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct in connection with the purchase or sale of any security`  IS FALSE
    `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct involving the making of a false filing with the Commission`  IS FALSE
    `subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities`  IS FALSE
    `the court order, judgment or decree restrains or enjoins the person at the time of such filing or sale`  IS FALSE
    `date the court order, judgment or decree was entered`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `subject to a final order of a State securities commission, a State bank or credit union supervisor, a State insurance commission, an appropriate Federal banking agency, the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission or the National Credit Union Administration`  IS FALSE
    `that final order bars the person from association with an entity regulated by such commission, authority, agency or officer`  IS FALSE
    `that final order bars the person from engaging in the business of securities, insurance or banking`  IS FALSE
    `that final order bars the person from engaging in savings association or credit union activities`  IS FALSE
    `that final order is based on a violation of a law or regulation prohibiting fraudulent, manipulative or deceptive conduct`  IS FALSE
    `date the final order was entered`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `subject to an order of the Commission under section 15(b) or 15B(c) of the Exchange Act or section 203(e) or (f) of the Investment Advisers Act`  IS FALSE
    `that Commission order suspends or revokes the person's registration as a broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser or funding portal`  IS FALSE
    `that Commission order places limitations on the activities, functions or operations of the person`  IS FALSE
    `that Commission order bars the person from being associated with any entity or from participating in the offering of any penny stock`  IS FALSE
    `date the Commission order under section 15(b), 15B(c) or Advisers Act 203(e) or (f) was entered`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of a scienter-based anti-fraud provision of the Federal securities laws`  IS FALSE
    `subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of section 5 of the Securities Act`  IS FALSE
    `that cease-and-desist order is in effect at the time of such filing or sale`  IS FALSE
    `date the Commission cease-and-desist order was entered`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `suspended or expelled from membership in, or suspended or barred from association with a member of, a registered national securities exchange or a registered national or affiliated securities association for conduct inconsistent with just and equitable principles of trade`  IS FALSE
    `date of the suspension or expulsion`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `filed as a registrant or issuer, or was named as an underwriter in, a registration statement or Regulation A offering statement that was the subject of a refusal order, stop order, or order suspending the Regulation A exemption`  IS FALSE
    `the subject, at the time of such filing or sale, of an investigation or proceeding to determine whether a stop order or suspension order should be issued`  IS FALSE
    `date of the refusal order, stop order or order suspending the Regulation A exemption`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `subject to a United States Postal Service false representation order`  IS FALSE
    `subject, at the time of such filing or sale, to a temporary restraining order or preliminary injunction with respect to conduct alleged by the United States Postal Service to constitute a scheme or device for obtaining money or property through the mail by means of false representations`  IS FALSE
    `date of the United States Postal Service false representation order`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `the court or regulatory authority that entered the relevant order, judgment or decree advised in writing that disqualification should not arise`  IS FALSE
    `the event occurred before the affiliation with the issuer arose`  IS FALSE
    `in control of the issuer`  IS FALSE
    `under common control with the issuer by a third party that was in control of the affiliated entity at the time of such events`  IS FALSE

@ref test fixture — an issuer, varying its closings, its holder counts and its prior sales
GIVEN `who`                IS A STRING
      `closings`           IS A LIST OF Closing
      `sold in the window` IS A NUMBER
      `sold before`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `reports filed`      IS A NUMBER
      `record holders`     IS A NUMBER
      `investors behind`   IS A NUMBER
      `people`             IS A LIST OF CoveredPerson
      `filed on`           IS A DATE
GIVETH AN IssuerProfile
`an issuer` `who` `closings` `sold in the window` `sold before` `reports filed` `record holders` `investors behind` `people` `filed on` MEANS IssuerProfile WITH
    name  IS `who`
    `organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia`  IS TRUE
    `subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`  IS FALSE
    `formerly subject to section 13 or 15(d) reporting, since terminated or suspended`  IS FALSE
    `an investment company as defined in section 3 of the Investment Company Act, or excluded from that definition by section 3(b) or section 3(c) of that Act`  IS FALSE
    `has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`  IS `sold before`
    `has filed with the Commission and provided to investors the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement`  IS TRUE
    `no specific business plan, or a business plan to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies`  IS FALSE
    `covered persons`  IS `people`
    `did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known that a disqualification existed`  IS FALSE
    `the Commission has determined that it is not necessary under the circumstances that an exemption be denied`  IS FALSE
    `closings in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`  IS `closings`
    `amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the 12-month period preceding the date of such offer or sale`  IS `sold in the window`
    `previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`  IS `sold before`
    `required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`  IS FALSE
    `annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part`  IS `reports filed`
    `holders of record`  IS `record holders`
    `investors who invested in the offering`  IS `investors behind`
    `total assets`  IS 50_000_000
    `all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6) repurchased, including any payment in full of debt securities or any complete redemption of redeemable securities`  IS FALSE
    `liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law`  IS FALSE
    `matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016`  IS FALSE
    `those matters disclosed`  IS TRUE
    `did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known of the existence of the undisclosed matter`  IS FALSE
    `previously failed to comply with the ongoing reporting requirements of § 227.202`  IS FALSE
    `date the offering statement was filed`  IS `filed on`
    `end of the fiscal year covered by the report`  IS YMD 2025 12 31

@ref test fixture — a complete § 227.201 disclosure
GIVETH A Disclosure
`a complete disclosure` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `the name, legal status, physical address and Web site of the issuer`  IS TRUE
    `the names of the directors and officers, their positions, tenure and business experience during the past three years`  IS TRUE
