    `a description of the purpose and intended use of the offering proceeds`  IS TRUE
    `a description of the process to complete the transaction or cancel an investment commitment`  IS TRUE
    `a statement that an investor who does not reconfirm after a material change will have the commitment cancelled and the funds returned`  IS TRUE
    `the price to the public of the securities or the method for determining the price`  IS TRUE
    `a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer`  IS TRUE
    `the name, SEC file number and CRD number of the intermediary`  IS TRUE
    `a description of the intermediary's financial interests in the issuer's transaction and in the issuer`  IS TRUE
    `a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer`  IS TRUE
    `a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years`  IS TRUE
    `a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold`  IS TRUE
    `a discussion of the issuer's financial condition`  IS TRUE
    `the financial statements and tax information required by paragraph (t)`  IS TRUE
    `any matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016`  IS TRUE
    `updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount`  IS TRUE
    `where on the issuer's Web site investors will be able to find the issuer's annual report, and by when`  IS TRUE
    `whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202`  IS TRUE
    `any material information necessary to make the statements made not misleading`  IS TRUE
    `any written communication or broadcast script provided in accordance with § 227.206 or § 230.241`  IS TRUE

@ref test fixture — an offering, varying its target, its deadlines and its notices
GIVEN `target`         IS A NUMBER
      `oversubscribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maximum`        IS A NUMBER
      `published on`   IS A DATE
      `deadline`       IS A DATE
      `committed`      IS A NUMBER
      `new deadline`   IS A DATE
      `notice given on` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN OfferingProfile
`an offering` `target` `oversubscribed` `maximum` `published on` `deadline` `committed` `new deadline` `notice given on` MEANS OfferingProfile WITH
    `target offering amount`  IS `target`
    `deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials`  IS `deadline`
    `the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount`  IS `oversubscribed`
    `maximum amount the issuer will accept`  IS `maximum`
    `date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform`  IS `published on`
    `sum of the investment commitments`  IS `committed`
    `the offering statement filed prior to the commencement of the offering`  IS TRUE
    `the disclosure provided`  IS `a complete disclosure`
    `conducted through an intermediary that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`  IS TRUE
    `conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform`  IS TRUE
    `more than one intermediary used in this offering`  IS FALSE
    `more than one intermediary used by the issuer for this capital raise`  IS FALSE
    `the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`  IS TRUE
    `the only failure to comply is with §§ 227.202, 227.203(a)(3) and 227.203(b)`  IS FALSE
    `the issuer knows that the investor has exceeded, or would exceed, the investor limits`  IS FALSE
    `a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer`  IS FALSE
    `date the material change notice was received by the investor`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `new offering deadline`  IS `new deadline`
    `date the notice of the new offering deadline was provided`  IS `notice given on`
    `notice given of the new, anticipated deadline of the offering`  IS TRUE
    `notice given of the right of investors to cancel investment commitments for any reason until 48 hours prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `notice given of whether the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `the offering completed`  IS TRUE

@ref test fixture — a transfer of restricted securities
GIVEN `issued on`   IS A DATE
      `transferred on` IS A DATE
      `to the issuer`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Transfer
`a transfer` `issued on` `transferred on` `to the issuer` MEANS Transfer WITH
    `date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6)`  IS `issued on`
    `date of the transfer`  IS `transferred on`
    `to the issuer of the securities`  IS `to the issuer`
    `to an accredited investor`  IS FALSE
    `as part of an offering registered with the Commission`  IS FALSE
    `to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent, to a trust controlled by the purchaser, to a trust created for the benefit of such a family member, or in connection with the death or divorce of the purchaser or other similar circumstance`  IS FALSE


§§ `Tests — the cases the regulation itself states or plainly implies`

-- --- § 227.100(a)(2), the four arithmetic corners of the investment limit ---
-- Every figure below is computed from the rule, not from a worked example, and
-- each corner exercises a different arm.

`a modest investor`      MEANS `an investor` "Ann"   TRUE  50_000    50_000    0 0 0
`an investor with income only` MEANS `an investor` "Ben" TRUE 150_000  80_000    0 0 0
`a comfortable investor` MEANS `an investor` "Cy"    TRUE  150_000   150_000   0 0 0
`a wealthy investor`     MEANS `an investor` "Dee"   TRUE  2_000_000 2_000_000 0 0 0
`an entity investor`     MEANS `an investor` "Eek Ltd" FALSE 0       0         1_000_000 900_000 0

-- Both quantities below the boundary: the five percent arm, floored at $2,500.
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `a modest investor` EQUALS 2_500

-- Income above, net worth below: still the five percent arm, on the GREATER of
-- the two. 5% of $150,000 = $7,500.
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `an investor with income only` EQUALS 7_500

-- Both at or above the boundary: the ten percent arm. 10% of $150,000.
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `a comfortable investor` EQUALS 15_000

-- The ten percent arm, capped: 10% of $2,000,000 is $200,000, "not to exceed
-- an amount sold of $124,000".
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `a wealthy investor` EQUALS `the investor ceiling`

-- F-INVLIMIT-NONNATURAL, measured. The SAME entity gets a limit of $100,000
-- under the staff reading (10% of $1,000,000 revenue) and $2,500 under the
-- regulation's own words (which give an entity no revenue-or-net-assets route,
-- so its annual income and net worth of zero put it on the floor). A
-- forty-fold difference on one investor is what the fork is worth.
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `an entity investor` EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `the investment limit for the investor` `the text alone`    `an entity investor` EQUALS 2_500
#EVAL   `the investment limit for the investor` `the staff reading` `an entity investor`
#EVAL   `the investment limit for the investor` `the text alone`    `an entity investor`

-- --- § 227.100(a)(1), the worked example from CFI 100.05 ------------------
-- "an issuer that closed $500,000 on 2025-06-15 and $4,500,000 on 2025-09-30
-- may offer only $500,000 on 2026-06-16, because only the first closing's
-- anniversary has passed."

`the first closing`  MEANS Closing WITH `date` IS YMD 2025 6 15, `amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6)` IS 500_000
`the second closing` MEANS Closing WITH `date` IS YMD 2025 9 30, `amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6)` IS 4_500_000

`an issuer that has closed twice` MEANS
    `an issuer` "Fig Inc" (LIST `the first closing`, `the second closing`) 5_000_000 TRUE 1 250 250 EMPTY (YMD 2025 1 2)

`the offering on the anniversary` MEANS
    `an offering` 500_000 FALSE 500_000 (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 8 1) 0 (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 6 1)

#ASSERT `amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing` `an issuer that has closed twice` (YMD 2026 6 16) EQUALS 4_500_000
#ASSERT `the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap` `the staff reading` `an issuer that has closed twice` `the offering on the anniversary` (YMD 2026 6 16) EQUALS 500_000

-- The day before, both closings are still inside their windows and there is no
-- headroom at all.
#ASSERT `the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap` `the staff reading` `an issuer that has closed twice` `the offering on the anniversary` (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS 0

-- --- § 227.201(t), including the (t)(3) proviso trap -----------------------

`a first-time issuer` MEANS `an issuer` "Gil Co" EMPTY 0 FALSE 0 0 0 EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 2)
`a repeat issuer`     MEANS `an issuer` "Hob Co" EMPTY 0 TRUE  1 0 0 EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 2)

`a small offering`  MEANS `an offering` 100_000   FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
`a medium offering` MEANS `an offering` 500_000   FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
`a large offering`  MEANS `an offering` 1_000_000 FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
`a huge offering`   MEANS `an offering` 2_000_000 FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2026 4 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)

#ASSERT `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a small offering` EQUALS `tax return information with financial statements certified by the principal executive officer`
#ASSERT `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a medium offering` EQUALS `financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`

-- THE TRAP. At $1,000,000 the answer depends on whether the issuer has sold
-- under section 4(a)(6) before. Read in citation order, paragraph (t)(3) says
-- "audited" for both; the proviso reverses that for a first-time issuer up to
-- $1,235,000. An encoding whose BRANCH follows the source's order gets the
-- first of these two wrong.
#ASSERT `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a large offering` EQUALS `financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`
#ASSERT `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a repeat issuer` `a large offering` EQUALS `financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`

-- Above the first-time-issuer ceiling the proviso stops helping.
#ASSERT `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a huge offering` EQUALS `financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer`

-- --- § 227.501, the one-year resale restriction ----------------------------

#ASSERT NOT `the transfer is permitted` (`a transfer` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT     `the transfer is permitted` (`a transfer` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT     `the transfer is permitted` (`a transfer` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE)
-- The boundary: the anniversary itself is outside the restricted period on the
-- reading taken here, and the day before it is inside.
#ASSERT     `the transfer is permitted` (`a transfer` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the transfer is permitted` (`a transfer` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) FALSE)

-- --- § 227.503, the lookbacks and the transition --------------------------

`a director convicted in 2023` MEANS
    `a covered person convicted of securities fraud` "Ivy" `a director, officer, general partner or managing member of the issuer` TRUE (YMD 2023 1 1)
`an issuer convicted in 2019` MEANS
    `a covered person convicted of securities fraud` "Jay Co" `the issuer itself` TRUE (YMD 2019 1 1)
`a director convicted in 2015` MEANS
    `a covered person convicted of securities fraud` "Kai" `a director, officer, general partner or managing member of the issuer` TRUE (YMD 2015 1 1)

-- A director's conviction carries a TEN-year lookback: 2023 is inside it.
#ASSERT `the covered person is disqualified` `a director convicted in 2023` (YMD 2026 1 2)
-- The ISSUER's own conviction carries a FIVE-year lookback: 2019 is outside it
-- as at 2026, even though a director's would not be.
#ASSERT NOT `the covered person is disqualified` `an issuer convicted in 2019` (YMD 2026 1 2)
-- And the same 2019 conviction, tested in 2023, IS inside the five years.
#ASSERT `the covered person is disqualified` `an issuer convicted in 2019` (YMD 2023 1 2)
-- § 227.503(b)(1): a conviction before 2016-05-16 never disqualifies, however
-- recent the filing.
#ASSERT NOT `the covered person is disqualified` `a director convicted in 2015` (YMD 2020 1 2)

-- --- § 227.202(b)(2), the crowdfunding-vehicle look-through --------------
-- One issuer, one annual report filed, one holder on the register, 350
-- investors behind a single crowdfunding vehicle.

`an issuer behind a crowdfunding vehicle` MEANS
    `an issuer` "Lox Inc" EMPTY 0 TRUE 1 1 350 EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 2)

-- Under § 227.100(d) the vehicle is one holder, and the register agrees, so
-- the reporting duty ends.
#ASSERT `the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting` `the text alone` `an issuer behind a crowdfunding vehicle`
-- Under CFI 202.02 the count looks through to the 350 investors, and it does
-- not. Same facts, opposite answers, and both are defensible readings of the
-- same part.
#ASSERT NOT `the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting` `the staff reading` `an issuer behind a crowdfunding vehicle`

-- --- § 227.400(a), the later-of registration date -------------------------

