    `date approved for membership by a registered national securities association`  IS `approved on`
    `nonresident`  IS FALSE
    `an information sharing arrangement in place between the Commission and the competent regulator`  IS FALSE
    `information previously submitted on Form Funding Portal has become inaccurate`  IS FALSE
    `date that information became inaccurate`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal`  IS FALSE
    `the succession is based solely on a change of the predecessor's date or state of incorporation, form of organization, or composition of a partnership`  IS FALSE
    `date of the succession`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `has ceased to operate as a funding portal`  IS FALSE
    `date the withdrawal was received by the Commission`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `a written consent and power of attorney appointing an agent in the United States obtained`  IS FALSE
    `the name and address of its United States agent for service of process furnished on Schedule C`  IS FALSE
    `a change of agent communicated promptly to the Commission through amendment of Schedule C`  IS FALSE
    `a successor agent for service of process promptly appointed where required`  IS FALSE
    `the written consent and power of attorney maintained as part of its books and records for at least three years after termination`  IS FALSE
    `certified on Schedule C that it can and will provide prompt access to its books and records and submit to onsite inspection and examination`  IS FALSE
    `an opinion of counsel provided that it can, as a matter of law, provide that access and submit to that inspection`  IS FALSE
    `a change in the legal or regulatory framework affecting that access or inspection`  IS FALSE
    `date of the change in the legal or regulatory framework`  IS YMD 1900 1 1
    `written policies and procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with the federal securities laws implemented`  IS TRUE
    `complies with the requirements of part 248 of this chapter as they apply to brokers`  IS TRUE
    `permits the examination and inspection of its business and business operations`  IS TRUE
    `the nine categories of records made and preserved for five years, the first two years in an easily accessible place`  IS TRUE
    `organizational documents made and preserved during the operation of the funding portal and of any successor`  IS TRUE
    `records produced, reproduced and maintained in the original, non-alterable format or as permitted under § 240.17a-4(f)`  IS TRUE
    `a written undertaking filed with the registered national securities association where a third party maintains the records`  IS TRUE
    `records furnished promptly to the Commission and the association on request`  IS TRUE
    `subject to the requirements of the Currency and Foreign Transactions Reporting Act of 1970`  IS FALSE
    `the retention period required by 31 CFR chapter X in years`  IS 0

-- Approval comes late: the approval date governs.
#ASSERT `the date the funding portal's registration becomes effective` (`a portal` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- Approval comes early: the thirtieth calendar day governs.
#ASSERT `the date the funding portal's registration becomes effective` (`a portal` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 5)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- --- § 227.404(f), "the longer period of time" ----------------------------

#ASSERT `the governing retention period in years` (`a portal` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 5)) EQUALS 5
#EVAL   `the governing retention period in years` (`a portal` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 5))

-- --- § 227.304(b), the early close ----------------------------------------
-- Published 2026-01-01; the original deadline is 2026-06-01; the issuer has
-- reached its $500,000 target and proposes a new deadline of 2026-03-02, with
-- notice given on 2026-02-20 — which is more than 21 days after publication
-- and more than five business days before the new deadline.

`an offering closing early` MEANS
    `an offering` 500_000 FALSE 500_000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) 500_000 (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 2 20)

-- The same offering with a new deadline only two days after the notice: the
-- five-business-day floor in paragraph (b)(3) is not met.
`an offering closing too fast` MEANS
    `an offering` 500_000 FALSE 500_000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) 500_000 (YMD 2026 2 22) (YMD 2026 2 20)

-- And with a new deadline only ten days after publication: the twenty-one-day
-- floor in paragraph (b)(1) is not met.
`an offering closing too soon` MEANS
    `an offering` 500_000 FALSE 500_000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) 500_000 (YMD 2026 1 11) (YMD 2026 1 2)

#ASSERT     `the issuer may close the offering early` `an offering closing early`
#ASSERT NOT `the issuer may close the offering early` `an offering closing too fast`
#ASSERT NOT `the issuer may close the offering early` `an offering closing too soon`

-- --- § 227.100(a), the exemption end to end -------------------------------

#ASSERT `the crowdfunding exemption is available` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a small offering` `a modest investor` 2_000 (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- The same everything, except that the investor is asked for $3,000 — more
-- than the $2,500 limit § 227.100(a)(2)(i) gives them. Paragraph (a)(2) is NOT
-- satisfied on its own terms:
#ASSERT NOT `100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded` `the staff reading` `a modest investor` 3_000

-- ... and yet the ISSUER's exemption survives, because Instruction 3 to
-- paragraph (a)(2) lets the issuer rely on the intermediary's § 227.303(b)
-- efforts so long as it does not know the limit is or would be exceeded. THIS
-- IS THE RULE AND NOT AN ENCODING SLIP, and it is worth being able to see: the
-- investor cap bites on the INTERMEDIARY, under § 227.303(b), and an issuer
-- that did not know keeps its exemption when the cap is breached. A first
-- draft of this test asserted the opposite and failed, which is how the
-- asymmetry got noticed.
#ASSERT `the crowdfunding exemption is available` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a small offering` `a modest investor` 3_000 (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- --- § 227.503 through § 227.100(b)(4) ------------------------------------

`an issuer with a disqualified director` MEANS
    `an issuer` "Nim Co" EMPTY 0 FALSE 0 0 0 (LIST `a director convicted in 2023`) (YMD 2026 1 2)

#ASSERT `no exemption is available because of a disqualification` `an issuer with a disqualified director`
#ASSERT `the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer` `the staff reading` `an issuer with a disqualified director`
#ASSERT NOT `the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer`

-- --- § 227.230.501(a)(5), the primary-residence arithmetic ----------------
-- $1,200,000 of assets outside the residence, a residence worth $600,000
-- carrying an $800,000 mortgage that stood at $700,000 sixty days ago. The
-- excess over fair market value is $200,000 (limb (C)); the sixty-day increase
-- is $100,000 (limb (B)); so net worth is $900,000 and the person is NOT an
-- accredited investor on the net-worth test, though the unadjusted arithmetic
-- would have said $1,200,000.
`a homeowner` MEANS InvestorProfile WITH
    name  IS "Ola"
    `a natural person`  IS TRUE
    `within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be`  IS FALSE
    `annual income for the calendar year`  IS 100_000
    `annual income for the investor's own fiscal year`  IS 100_000
    `revenue for the most recent fiscal year`  IS 0
    `net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end`  IS 0
    `total assets other than the primary residence`  IS 1_200_000
    `total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence`  IS 0
    `estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale`  IS 600_000
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale`  IS 800_000
    `indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale`  IS 700_000
    `the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence`  IS FALSE
    `the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities`  IS FALSE
    `that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010`  IS FALSE
    `qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired`  IS FALSE
    `held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010`  IS FALSE
    `net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments`  IS 1_200_000
    `individual income in each of the two most recent years`  IS 100_000
    `joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years`  IS 0
    `a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year`  IS TRUE
    `aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months`  IS 0
    `annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse`  IS FALSE
    `the aggregate investment of the investor spouses`  IS 0

#ASSERT `the investor's net worth` `a homeowner` EQUALS 900_000
#ASSERT NOT `the investor is an accredited investor` `a homeowner`
#EVAL   `the investor's net worth` `a homeowner`

-- --- § 227.304(c), the reconfirmation chain, exercised --------------------
-- A DEONTIC value cannot be EQUALS-compared in an #ASSERT, so the chain is
-- exercised with #TRACE instead. The residual is the story: the intermediary
-- gives notice, the investor reconfirms, and nothing is left owed.

`an offering with a material change` MEANS OfferingProfile WITH
    `target offering amount`  IS 500_000
    `deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials`  IS YMD 2026 6 1
    `the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount`  IS FALSE
    `maximum amount the issuer will accept`  IS 500_000
    `date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform`  IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `sum of the investment commitments`  IS 400_000
    `the offering statement filed prior to the commencement of the offering`  IS TRUE
    `the disclosure provided`  IS `a complete disclosure`
    `conducted through an intermediary that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`  IS TRUE
    `conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform`  IS TRUE
    `more than one intermediary used in this offering`  IS FALSE
    `more than one intermediary used by the issuer for this capital raise`  IS FALSE
    `the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part`  IS TRUE
    `the only failure to comply is with §§ 227.202, 227.203(a)(3) and 227.203(b)`  IS FALSE
    `the issuer knows that the investor has exceeded, or would exceed, the investor limits`  IS FALSE
    `a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer`  IS TRUE
    `date the material change notice was received by the investor`  IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `new offering deadline`  IS YMD 2026 6 1
    `date the notice of the new offering deadline was provided`  IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `notice given of the new, anticipated deadline of the offering`  IS TRUE
    `notice given of the right of investors to cancel investment commitments for any reason until 48 hours prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `notice given of whether the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline`  IS TRUE
    `the offering completed`  IS TRUE

`a reconfirmed commitment` MEANS CommitmentProfile WITH
    `investor`  IS `a modest investor`
    `amount of the investment commitment`  IS 2_000
    `date the investment commitment was made`  IS YMD 2026 2 1
    `reconfirmed within five business days of receipt of the notice`  IS TRUE

`an abandoned commitment` MEANS CommitmentProfile WITH
    `investor`  IS `a modest investor`
    `amount of the investment commitment`  IS 2_000
    `date the investment commitment was made`  IS YMD 2026 2 1
    `reconfirmed within five business days of receipt of the notice`  IS FALSE

-- The happy path: notice, then reconfirmation, both inside their windows.
#TRACE `the material change reconfirmation chain` `an offering with a material change` `a reconfirmed commitment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the intermediary` DOES `give or send the investor notice of the material change` AT 1
    PARTY `the investor`     DOES `reconfirm the investment commitment` AT 3

-- The investor never reconfirms: what is left standing is the intermediary's
-- notify-and-refund chain, which is exactly what § 227.304(c)(1)(i)-(ii) says
-- happens next.
#TRACE `the material change reconfirmation chain` `an offering with a material change` `an abandoned commitment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the intermediary` DOES `give or send the investor notice of the material change` AT 1

#EVAL `the issuer may close the offering early` `an offering closing early`
#EVAL `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a first-time issuer` `a large offering`
#EVAL `the financial statements required` `the staff reading` `a repeat issuer` `a large offering`
#EVAL `the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap` `the staff reading` `an issuer that has closed twice` `the offering on the anniversary` (YMD 2026 6 16)
